Object.assign(window.TEM8_DICTIONARY, {"playwright":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/playwright__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/playwright__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪraɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who writes plays for the theatre, television or radio","cn":"剧作家","ex":{"en":"Which playwright wrote ‘Doctor Faustus’?","cn":"哪位剧作家写了《浮士德博士》?"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"剧作家","en":"A playwright is a person who writes plays."}]}},"plump":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plump__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plump__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"plʌmp","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having a soft, round body; slightly fat","cn":"丰腴的；微胖的","ex":{"en":"a short, plump woman","cn":"一个矮胖的女人"}},{"en":"looking soft, full and attractive to use or eat","cn":"松软的；丰满的；饱满的","ex":{"en":"plump cushions","cn":"松软的垫子"}},{"en":"to make something larger, softer and rounder","cn":"使变大；使更软；使更圆","ex":{"en":"He leaned forward while the nurse plumped up his pillows.","cn":"他往前够了够身子，让护士把枕头拍松了。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"丰满的；胖乎乎的；圆滚滚的","en":"You can describe someone or something as plump to indicate that they are rather fat or rounded.","ex":{"en":"Maria was small and plump with a mass of curly hair","cn":"玛丽亚身材矮小丰满，一头卷发。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（通过摇抖或拍打）使膨松，使松软鼓起","en":"If you plump a pillow or cushion, you shake it and hit it gently so that it goes back into a rounded shape.","ex":{"en":"She panics when people pop in unexpectedly, rushing round plumping cushions.","cn":"一群人冷不防地冒出来，跑来跑去地拍松垫子，这把她吓坏了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（常指经过犹豫或深思熟虑后）选择，选中","en":"If you plump for someone or something, you choose them, often after hesitating or thinking carefully.","ex":{"en":"I think Tessa should plump for Malcolm, her long-suffering admirer.","cn":"我想特莎应该选择长期默默爱慕她的马尔科姆。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He leaned forward while the nurse plumped up his pillows.","cn":"他往前够了够身子，让护士把枕头拍松了。"},{"en":"a short, plump woman","cn":"一个矮胖的女人"}]},"planets":{"lemma":"planet","media":{"uk":"media/uk/planet__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/planet__us_1.mp3"}},"planting":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/planting__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/planting__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplɑːntɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an act of planting something; something that has just been planted","cn":"种植；栽种；栽种物","ex":{"en":"The Tree Council promotes tree planting.","cn":"林木委员会倡导植树造林。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The Tree Council promotes tree planting.","cn":"林木委员会倡导植树造林。"},{"en":"These bushes are fairly recent plantings.","cn":"这些灌木丛是最近栽植的。"}],"base":"plant"},"planes":{"lemma":"plane","media":{"uk":"media/uk/plan__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plan__us_1.mp3"}},"plate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pleɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a flat, usually round, dish that you put food on","cn":"盘子；碟子","g":"[countable]","sc":"food","ex":{"en":"sandwiches on a plate","cn":"盘子上的三明治"}},{"en":"the amount of food that you can put on a plate","cn":"一盘所盛之量；一盘","g":"[countable]","sc":"food","ex":{"en":"a plate of sandwiches","cn":"一盘三明治"}},{"en":"a whole main course of a meal, served on one plate","cn":"一道主菜","g":"[countable]","lab":"especially North American English","sc":"food","ex":{"en":"Try the seafood plate.","cn":"尝尝这道海鲜吧。"}},{"en":"a thin flat piece of metal, used especially to join or make something stronger","cn":"（金属）板条，板","g":"[countable]","sc":"for strength","ex":{"en":"The tanks were mainly constructed of steel plates.","cn":"这些坦克车主要是用钢板制造的。"}},{"en":"a flat piece of metal with some information on it, for example somebody’s name","cn":"（刻有名字等的）金属牌子","g":"[countable]","sc":"for information","ex":{"en":"A brass plate beside the door said ‘Dr Alan Tate’.","cn":"门旁的铜牌上写着“艾伦·泰特医生”。"}},{"en":"the pieces of metal or plastic at the front and back of a vehicle with numbers and letters on it","cn":"（车辆）牌照，号牌；车牌","g":"[usually plural]","sc":"on vehicle"},{"en":"ordinary metal that is covered with a thin layer of silver or gold","cn":"镀金（或镀银）的金属","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"silver/gold","ex":{"en":"The cutlery is plate, not solid silver.","cn":"这套餐具是镀银的，不是纯银的。"}},{"en":"dishes, bowls, etc. that are made of silver or gold","cn":"金质（或银质）餐具","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"silver/gold","ex":{"en":"the family plate","cn":"家庭餐盘"}},{"en":"one of the thin flat pieces of horn or bone that cover and protect an animal","cn":"板；骨板","g":"[countable]","lab":"biology","sc":"on animal","ex":{"en":"the armadillo’s protective shell of bony plates","cn":"犰狳的一层防护性骨板"}},{"en":"one of the very large pieces of rock that form the earth’s surface and move slowly","cn":"板块","g":"[countable]","sc":"geology","ex":{"en":"the Pacific plate","cn":"太平洋板块"}},{"en":"a photograph that is used as a picture in a book, especially one that is printed on a separate page on high quality paper","cn":"书籍插图照片；（尤指优质纸上的）整页插图","g":"[countable]","sc":"printing/photography","ex":{"en":"The book includes 55 colour plates.","cn":"本书有 55 幅彩色插图。"}},{"en":"a sheet of metal, plastic, etc. that has been treated so that words or pictures can be printed from it","cn":"（印刷用的）印版，图版","g":"[countable]","sc":"printing/photography","ex":{"en":"a printing plate","cn":"印版"}},{"en":"a thin sheet of glass, metal, etc. that is covered with chemicals so that it reacts to light and can form an image, used in larger or older cameras","cn":"（玻璃、金属等）底片，感光板","g":"[countable]","sc":"printing/photography"},{"en":"a thin piece of plastic with wire or artificial teeth attached to it which fits inside your mouth in order to make your teeth straight","cn":"假牙托；托牙板；假牙床","g":"[countable]","sc":"in mouth"},{"en":"the place where the person hitting the ball stands and where they must return to after running around all the bases","cn":"本垒板；本垒","g":"[singular]","lab":"North American English","sc":"in baseball"},{"en":"a flat dish that is used to collect money from people in a church","cn":"奉献盘；捐款盘","g":"[singular]","sc":"in church"},{"en":"to cover a metal with a thin layer of another metal, especially gold or silver","cn":"电镀（尤指镀金或镀银）","ex":{"en":"a silver ring plated with gold","cn":"一枚镀金的银戒指"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to cover something with sheets of metal or another hard substance","cn":"为…加设护板；（用金属板等）覆盖","ex":{"en":"The walls of the vault were plated with steel.","cn":"保险库的墙壁都装了钢板。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to serve food on a plate","cn":"摆盘","ex":{"en":"How the food is plated up is of vital importance in high-end restaurants.","cn":"对于高档餐厅来说，食物的摆盘方式至关重要。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"盘；碟","en":"A plate is a round or oval flat dish that is used to hold food.","ex":{"en":"Anita pushed her plate away; she had eaten virtually nothing.","cn":"安妮塔把自己的盘子推开;她几乎什么都没吃。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（尤指用于机械或建筑上金属制的）平板，薄板","en":"A plate is a flat piece of metal, especially on machinery or a building."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（通常置于办公室或住宅门边上的）金属姓名牌","en":"A plate is a small, flat piece of metal with someone's name written on it, which you usually find beside the front door of an office or house."},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"（车辆的）号码牌，牌照","en":"On a road vehicle, the plates are the panels at the front and back which display the license number in the United States, and the registration number in Britain.","ex":{"en":"...dusty-looking cars with New Jersey plates.","cn":"落满灰尘、挂着新泽西州牌照的汽车"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（尤指银或金质的）餐具","en":"Plate is dishes, bowls, and cups that are made of precious metal, especially silver or gold.","ex":{"en":"...gold and silver plate, jewellery, and roomfuls of antique furniture.","cn":"金银餐具、珠宝，还有整屋整屋的古董家具"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（印刷用的）印版，图版","en":"In printing, a plate is a sheet of metal which is carved or specially treated with chemicals so that it can be used to print text or pictures."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（摄影中的）感光板，（玻璃）干版","en":"In photography, a plate is a thin sheet of glass that is covered with a layer of chemicals which react to the light and on which an image can be formed."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（书中的）整版插图","en":"A plate in a book is a picture or photograph which takes up a whole page and is usually printed on better quality paper than the rest of the book.","ex":{"en":"Fermor's book has 55 colour plates.","cn":"弗莫尔的书里有55页整版彩色插图。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（显微镜下的长方形）载物片，玻璃片","en":"In a microscope, the plate is a small rectangular piece of glass onto which you put a small amount of the substance that you want to look at. You then slide the plate under the microscope to look at the substance."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"假牙托；（牙）托基","en":"A dental plate is a piece of plastic which is shaped to fit inside a person's mouth and which a set of false teeth is attached to."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（地质学中的大陆）板块","en":"In geology, a plate is a large piece of the earth's surface, perhaps as large as a continent, which moves very slowly.","ex":{"en":"The United States Geological Survey has revealed that the earthquake was not caused by a simple horizontal movement of one plate past another.","cn":"美国地质调查局揭示了此次地震并非由大陆板块间简单的水平交错运动所引起。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（棒球运动中）the plate 同 home plate","en":"In baseball, the plate is the same as the home plate."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"有很多工作要做；有很多事要处理","en":"If you have enough on your plate or have a lot on your plate, you have a lot of work to do or a lot of things to deal with.","ex":{"en":"We have enough on our plate. There is plenty of work to be done on what we have.","cn":"我们有很多工作要做。仅是手头现有的事情就已经有的忙了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"把…拱手奉送给","en":"If you say that someone has things handed to them on a plate, you disapprove of them because they get good things easily.","ex":{"en":"Even the presidency was handed to him on a plate.","cn":"他甚至连总统之位都是得来全不费工夫。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"A brass plate beside the door said ‘Dr Alan Tate’.","cn":"门旁的铜牌上写着“艾伦 · 泰特医生”。"},{"en":"Earthquakes are caused by two tectonic plates bumping into each other.","cn":"地震是由两块地壳构造板块互相碰撞造成的。"}]},"pleasant":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/pleasant__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/pleasant__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleznt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"fun, attractive, or giving pleasure","cn":"愉快的；给人快乐的","ex":{"en":"a pleasant evening/atmosphere/walk","cn":"愉快的夜晚／气氛／散步"}},{"en":"friendly and polite","cn":"友好的；和善的；文雅的","ex":{"en":"a pleasant young man","cn":"彬彬有礼的年轻人"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"令人愉快的；舒适的；合意的","en":"Something that is pleasant is nice, enjoyable, or attractive.","ex":{"en":"I've got a pleasant little apartment","cn":"我有一套舒适的小公寓。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"友好的；可亲的；讨人喜欢的","en":"Someone who is pleasant is friendly and likeable.","ex":{"en":"The woman had a pleasant face","cn":"这位女士面相和善。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"What a pleasant surprise!","cn":"这真是一桩令人又惊又喜的事！"},{"en":"I was pleasantly surprised by my exam results.","cn":"我的考试成绩真让我喜出望外。"}]},"pleasure":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/pleasure__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/pleasure__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleʒə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a state of feeling or being happy or satisfied","cn":"高兴；快乐；愉快；欣慰；满意","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"His eyes lit up with pleasure.","cn":"他高兴得双眼放光。"}},{"en":"the activity of enjoying yourself, especially in contrast to working","cn":"玩乐；休闲","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Are you in Paris on business or pleasure?","cn":"你来巴黎是公干还是游玩？"}},{"en":"a thing that makes you happy or satisfied","cn":"乐事；快事","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"the simple pleasures of the countryside","cn":"乡村淳朴的乐趣"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"愉快；高兴；快乐；满足","en":"If something gives you pleasure, you get a feeling of happiness, satisfaction, or enjoyment from it.","ex":{"en":"Watching sport gave him great pleasure","cn":"观看体育比赛给他以极大的愉悦。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（尤指工作、职责之外的）娱乐，消遣","en":"Pleasure is the activity of enjoying yourself, especially rather than working or doing what you have a duty to do.","ex":{"en":"He mixed business and pleasure in a perfect and dynamic way","cn":"他以互动的方式将工作和娱乐完美地结合起来。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"乐趣；乐事；给人愉快的事物","en":"A pleasure is an activity, experience or aspect of something that you find very enjoyable or satisfying.","ex":{"en":"Watching TV is our only pleasure.","cn":"看电视是我们唯一的乐事。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"很高兴见到…/…莅临的荣幸","en":"If you meet someone for the first time, you can say, as a way of being polite, that it is a pleasure to meet them. You can also ask for the pleasure of someone's company as a polite and formal way of inviting them somewhere.","ex":{"en":"'A pleasure to meet you, sir,' he said","cn":"他说：“先生，很高兴见到您。”"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（受到感谢时的一种礼貌回答）别客气，不用谢，是我的荣幸","en":"You can say 'It's a pleasure ' or 'My pleasure ' as a polite way of replying to someone who has just thanked you for doing something.","ex":{"en":"'Thanks very much anyhow.' — 'It's a pleasure.'","cn":"“无论怎样，非常感谢。”——“别客气。”"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"非常乐意；愿意效劳","en":"You can say 'With pleasure ' as a polite way of saying that you are very willing to do something.","ex":{"en":"'Could you photocopy the advert and put it in the post to us?' — 'With pleasure John.'","cn":"“你能把广告影印一下寄给我们吗？”——“当然可以，约翰。”"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"You've never been to this area before? Then you're in for a real treat.","cn":"你以前从来没有到过这一地区？那么你一定会喜之不尽。"},{"en":"‘May I sit here?’ ‘Yes, with pleasure.’ “","cn":"我可以坐在这儿吗？” “当然可以。”"}]},"plan":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plan__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plan__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"plæn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"something that you intend to do or achieve","cn":"计划；打算","sc":"intention","ex":{"en":"Do you have any plans for the summer?","cn":"这个夏天你有什么打算？"}},{"en":"a set of things to do in order to achieve something, especially one that has been considered in detail in advance","cn":"（详细）规划，方案；精心安排","sc":"arrangement","ex":{"en":"an action plan","cn":"行动方案"}},{"en":"a detailed map of a building, town, etc.","cn":"（建筑、城镇等的）详图","sc":"map","ex":{"en":"Do you have a plan of the museum?","cn":"你有博物馆的详图吗？"}},{"en":"a detailed drawing of a machine, building, etc. that shows its size, shape and measurements","cn":"（机器、建筑等的）设计图，平面图；图解","g":"[usually plural]","lab":"specialist","sc":"drawing","ex":{"en":"The original plans of the building have not survived.","cn":"这栋建筑的原始设计图没有保存下来。"}},{"en":"a diagram that shows how something will be arranged","cn":"分布图；示意图","sc":"drawing","ex":{"en":"a seating plan (= showing where each person will sit, for example at a dinner)","cn":"座位安排示意图"}},{"en":"a way of investing money for the future or buying insurance for something","cn":"（投资或保险的）计划，方案","sc":"money","ex":{"en":"a savings plan","cn":"储蓄计划"}},{"en":"to make detailed arrangements for something you want to do in the future","cn":"精心安排；计划；谋划","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"make arrangements","ex":{"en":"to plan a trip","cn":"计划一次旅行"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to intend or expect to do something","cn":"打算；期待","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"intend/expect","ex":{"en":"We hadn't planned on going anywhere this evening.","cn":"我们今晚没打算外出。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make a design or an outline for something","cn":"设计；安排；组织；策划","g":"[transitive]","sc":"design","ex":{"en":"to plan an essay/a garden","cn":"构思一篇文章；设计一个花园"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"计划；规划；方案","en":"A plan is a method of achieving something that you have worked out in detail beforehand.","ex":{"en":"The three leaders had worked out a peace plan","cn":"3位领导人已制订出了一个和平方案。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"计划；筹划；谋划","en":"If you plan what you are going to do, you decide in detail what you are going to do, and you intend to do it.","ex":{"en":"If you plan what you're going to eat, you reduce your chances of overeating","cn":"如果计划一下要吃什么，就有可能不会吃得过多。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"（有做某一特定事的）计划，打算，意向","en":"If you have plans, you are intending to do a particular thing.","ex":{"en":"'I'm sorry,' she said. 'I have plans for tonight.'","cn":"“抱歉，”她说，“我今晚有安排了。”"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"设计；绘制…的图样（或图表）","en":"When you plan something that you are going to make, build, or create, you decide what the main parts of it will be and do a drawing of how it should be made.","ex":{"en":"We are planning a new kitchen.","cn":"我们在设计新厨房。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"平面图；详图；图表","en":"A plan of something that is going to be built or made is a detailed diagram or drawing of it.","ex":{"en":"...when you have drawn a plan of the garden.","cn":"当你画出花园的平面图后"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：plan on plan out"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The government has announced plans to create one million new training places.","cn":"政府已经宣布开设一百万个新培训名额的计划。"},{"en":"We're planning a trip to France in the spring — are you interested?","cn":"我们打算春天去法国旅游。你有意去吗？"}]},"pliers":{"media":{"img":["media/ldoce/img/pliers.jpg","media/pic/tools_diy_comp.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/pliers__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/pliers__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplaɪəz","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a metal tool with handles, used for holding things and twisting and cutting wire","cn":"钳子；夹钳","ex":{"en":"a pair of pliers","cn":"一把钳子"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"钳子；老虎钳","en":"Pliers are a tool with two handles at one end and two hard, flat, metal parts at the other. Pliers are used for holding or pulling out things such as nails, or for bending or cutting wire."}]},"examples":[{"en":"a pair of pliers","cn":"一把钳子"}]},"plural":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplʊərəl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a form of a noun or verb that refers to more than one person or thing","cn":"（名词或动词的）复数，复数形式","ex":{"en":"The plural of ‘child’ is ‘children’.","cn":"child 一词的复数形式是 children。"}},{"en":"connected with or having the plural form","cn":"复数的；复数形式的","lab":"grammar","ex":{"en":"Most plural nouns in English end in ‘s’.","cn":"英语中多数复数名词以 s 结尾。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"relating to more than one","cn":"多样的；多元的","ex":{"en":"a plural society (= one with more than one racial, religious, etc. group)","cn":"多元社会"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"复数的；复数形式的","en":"The plural form of a word is the form that is used when referring to more than one person or thing.","ex":{"en":"'Data' is the Latin plural form of 'datum'.","cn":"data 在拉丁文中是 datum 的复数形式。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"复数；复数形式","en":"The plural of a noun is the form of it that is used to refer to more than one person or thing.","ex":{"en":"What is the plural of 'person'?","cn":"person 的复数形式是什么？"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"多元的；多种群体的","en":"A plural society or system involves different kinds of people.","ex":{"en":"Britain is a plural society in which the secular predominates","cn":"英国是个世俗主导的多元社会。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plural__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plural__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The plural of ‘child’ is ‘children’. * child","cn":"一词的复数形式是 children。"},{"en":"Most plural nouns in English end in ‘s’.","cn":"英语中多数复数名词以 s 结尾。"}]},"plane":{"media":{"img":["media/ldoce/img/plane.jpg","media/pic/airliner_comp.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/plane__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plane__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pleɪn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a flying vehicle with wings and one or more engines","cn":"飞机","lab":"British English also","ex":{"en":"a passenger/fighter/military/private plane","cn":"客机；战斗机；军机；私人飞机"}},{"en":"any flat or level surface, or an imaginary flat surface through or joining material objects","cn":"平面","lab":"geometry","ex":{"en":"the horizontal/vertical plane","cn":"水平／垂直平面"}},{"en":"a level of thought, existence or development","cn":"（思想、存在或发展的）水平，程度，阶段，境界","ex":{"en":"With practice, an athlete can reach a higher plane of achievement.","cn":"通过练习，运动员可以取得更好的成绩。"}},{"en":"a tool with a blade (= sharp metal part) set in a flat surface, used for making the surface of wood smooth by cutting very thin layers off it","cn":"木工刨；刨子"},{"en":"completely flat; level","cn":"平的；平坦的","ex":{"en":"a plane surface","cn":"平面"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"to make a piece of wood smoother or flatter with a plane","cn":"（用刨子）刨平","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Plane the surface down first.","cn":"首先要把表面刨平。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to fly without moving the wings, especially high up in the air","cn":"滑翔","g":"[intransitive]","pos":"verb"},{"en":"to move quickly across water, only just touching the surface","cn":"擦着水面疾驶","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The boat planed past in clouds of spray.","cn":"船在浪花中缓缓驶过。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"飞机","en":"A plane is a vehicle with wings and one or more engines, which can fly through the air.","ex":{"en":"He had plenty of time to catch his plane","cn":"他有足够的时间赶飞机。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（可能带有斜度的）平面","en":"A plane is a flat, level surface which may be sloping at a particular angle.","ex":{"en":"...a building with angled planes.","cn":"带有坡面的建筑物"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"（想象中的）平面","en":"If a number of points are in the same plane, one line or one flat surface could pass through them all.","ex":{"en":"All the planets orbit the Sun in roughly the same plane, round its equator.","cn":"所有的行星大致在同一平面上绕太阳赤道运转。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（精神的）水平，水准，层次","en":"If you say that something is on a higher plane, you mean that it is more spiritual or less concerned with ordinary things.","ex":{"en":"...life on a higher plane of existence","cn":"更高境界的生活"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"木工刨；刨子","en":"A plane is a tool that has a flat bottom with a sharp blade in it. You move the plane over a piece of wood in order to remove thin pieces of its surface."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"刨；刨平；刨光","en":"If you plane a piece of wood, you make it smaller or smoother by using a plane.","ex":{"en":"She watches him plane the surface of a walnut board","cn":"她看着他刨平一块胡桃木板。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（轻触水面）疾驶，滑行","en":"If something such as a boat planes across water, it moves quickly across the water, just touching the surface.","ex":{"en":"All four of the boats planed across the Solent with the greatest of ease.","cn":"4艘船都极其自如地掠过索伦特海峡。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"悬铃木","en":"A plane or a plane tree is a large tree with broad leaves which often grows in towns."},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：plane down"}]},"examples":[{"en":"I caught the next plane to Dublin.","cn":"我赶上了下一班飞机去都柏林。"},{"en":"The plane took off an hour late.","cn":"飞机延迟了一小时起飞。"}]},"plenty":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plenty__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plenty__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplenti","pos":"pronoun","senses":[{"en":"a large amount; as much or as many as you need","cn":"大量；众多；充足","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"plenty of eggs/money/time","cn":"充裕的鸡蛋／钱／时间"}},{"en":"a lot","cn":"大量；许多","ex":{"en":"We have plenty more of them in the warehouse.","cn":"我们仓库里这些东西还多得很。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"more than big, long, etc. enough","cn":"足够有余","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"The rope was plenty long enough to reach the ground.","cn":"这根绳子长及地面依然有余。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"a lot; very","cn":"非常；十分；很","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"We talked plenty about our kids.","cn":"我们谈了很多关于孩子的事。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"a situation in which there is a large supply of food, money, etc.","cn":"富裕；充裕","ex":{"en":"Everyone is happier in times of plenty.","cn":"在富足的岁月里，每个人都比较快乐。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a lot of","cn":"很多；大量","ex":{"en":"There's plenty room for all of you!","cn":"这里有足够的地方容纳你们所有人！"},"pos":"determiner"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"QUANT 数量词","cn":"（尤指足够的或超出需要的）丰富，充足，大量","en":"If there is plenty of something, there is a large amount of it. If there are plenty of things, there are many of them. Plenty is used especially to indicate that there is enough of something, or more than you need.","ex":{"en":"There was still plenty of time to take Jill out for pizza","cn":"还有充裕的时间带吉尔出去吃比萨饼。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"富裕；富足；繁荣","en":"Plenty is a situation in which people have a lot to eat or a lot of money to live on.","ex":{"en":"You are all fortunate to be growing up in a time of peace and plenty.","cn":"你们都很幸运，成长在和平富足的时代。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"（用于形容词或副词前）非常，十分，很","en":"You use plenty in front of adjectives or adverbs to emphasize the degree of the quality they are describing.","ex":{"en":"The water looked plenty deep","cn":"这水看起来很深。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"丰富地；充足地；大量地","en":"If there are things in plenty, those things exist or happen in large amounts or numbers.","ex":{"en":"There were thrills in plenty on Saturday at Terrassa, where Germany won the gold medal","cn":"周六的塔拉萨充满着紧张兴奋的气氛，德国队在此赢得了金牌。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘Do we need more milk?’ ‘No, there's plenty in the fridge.’ “","cn":"我们要不要再买些牛奶？” “不必了。冰箱里还多着呢。”"},{"en":"Everyone is happier in times of plenty.","cn":"在富足的岁月里，每个人都比较快乐。"}]},"placeholder":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/placeholder__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/placeholder__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪshəʊldə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a symbol or piece of text that temporarily replaces something that is missing","cn":"（临时替代缺失部分的）占位符，占位文字","lab":"specialist"},{"en":"an item which is necessary in a sentence, but does not have real meaning, for example the word ‘it’ in ‘It’s a shame she left.’","cn":"位标（句子中必要但无实际意义的词项，如 It’s a shame she left 中的 it）","lab":"linguistics"}]}},"pleased":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/pleased__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/pleased__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pliːzd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"feeling happy about something","cn":"高兴；满意；愉快","ex":{"en":"You're coming? I'm so pleased.","cn":"你要来呀？我太高兴了。"}},{"en":"happy or willing to do something","cn":"高兴，乐于（做某事）","lab":"especially British English","ex":{"en":"We are always pleased to be able to help.","cn":"我们一向乐意能帮忙。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"高兴的；喜欢的；满意的","en":"If you are pleased, you are happy about something or satisfied with something.","ex":{"en":"Felicity seemed pleased at the suggestion","cn":"费莉西蒂好像对这个建议很满意。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"高兴（做…）的；乐意（做…）的","en":"If you say you will be pleased to do something, you are saying in a polite way that you are willing to do it.","ex":{"en":"We will be pleased to answer any questions you may have","cn":"我们将很乐意回答你们可能想问的任何问题。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（对…）满意的；（对…）赞赏的","en":"You can tell someone that you are pleased with something they have done in order to express your approval.","ex":{"en":"I'm pleased with the way things have been going","cn":"我很满意事情的进展。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"不高兴的；不满意的","en":"If someone is not too pleased or is none too pleased, they are annoyed about something or do not think something is acceptable.","ex":{"en":"I was not too pleased with the record you sent me","cn":"我对你寄给我的唱片不太满意。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"高兴（地告诉或得知）的","en":"When you are about to give someone some news which you know will please them, you can say that you are pleased to tell them the news or that they will be pleased to hear it.","ex":{"en":"I'm pleased to say that he is now doing well","cn":"我很高兴地说，他现在一切都好。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（用于正式信函中）意欲（做…）的，决意（做…）的","en":"In official letters, people often say they will be pleased to do something, as a polite way of introducing what they are going to do or inviting people to do something.","ex":{"en":"We will be pleased to delete the charge from the original invoice","cn":"我们决定将这笔费用从原始发票上删去。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"对自己满意；（尤指）自鸣得意，飘飘然","en":"If someone seems very satisfied with something they have done, you can say that they are pleased with themselves, especially if you think they are more satisfied than they should be.","ex":{"en":"He was pleased with himself for having remembered her name","cn":"他为自己记住了她的名字得意起来。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"见到你很高兴；幸会；认识你很高兴","en":"You can say 'Pleased to meet you' as a polite way of greeting someone who you are meeting for the first time."}]},"examples":[{"en":"He did not look too pleased when I told him.","cn":"我告诉他时，他似乎不是很高兴。"},{"en":"I am pleased to inform you that the book you ordered has arrived.","cn":"谨此欣然奉告，您所订的书已到。"}],"base":"please"},"player":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/player__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/player__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who takes part in a game or sport","cn":"游戏者；运动员；参赛选手","ex":{"en":"a football/tennis/chess player","cn":"足球／网球／国际象棋选手"}},{"en":"a company or person involved in a particular area of business or politics","cn":"（商业或政治方面的）参与者，竞争者，玩家","ex":{"en":"The company has emerged as a major player in the London property market.","cn":"那家公司已崭露头角，成为伦敦房地产市场的主要竞争者。"}},{"en":"a machine for producing the sound or pictures that have been recorded on CDs, etc.","cn":"播放机","ex":{"en":"a DVD/CD player","cn":"数字影碟／光碟播放机"}},{"en":"a person who plays a musical instrument","cn":"演奏者","ex":{"en":"a trumpet/bass player","cn":"小号手；贝司手"}},{"en":"an actor","cn":"演员","lab":"old-fashioned","ex":{"en":"Phoenix Players present ‘Romeo and Juliet’.","cn":"凤凰剧社献演《罗密欧与朱丽叶》。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"运动员；选手；参加运动者","en":"A player in a sport or game is a person who takes part, either as a job or for fun.","ex":{"en":"...his greatness as a player","cn":"他作为运动员的伟大之处"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（乐器）演奏者","en":"You can use player to refer to a musician. For example, a piano player is someone who plays the piano.","ex":{"en":"...a professional trumpet player.","cn":"职业小号手"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"重要参与者","en":"If a person, country, or organization is a player in something, they are involved in it and important in it.","ex":{"en":"Big business has become a major player in the art market","cn":"大公司已成为艺术市场上的重要力量。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"演员；表演者","en":"A player is an actor.","ex":{"en":"...a company of players","cn":"一群演员"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The company has emerged as a major player in the London property market.","cn":"那家公司已崭露头角，成为伦敦物业市场的主要竞争者。"},{"en":"Phoenix Players present ‘Romeo and Juliet’.","cn":"凤凰剧社献演《罗密欧与朱丽叶》。"}]},"planning":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/planning__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/planning__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplænɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act or process of making plans for something","cn":"计划制订；规划过程","ex":{"en":"The department is responsible for all financial planning.","cn":"该部门负责所有财务规划。"}},{"en":"the control of the development of towns and their buildings, roads, etc. so that they can be pleasant and convenient places for people to live in","cn":"规划：控制城镇及其建筑物，道路等的发展，使之成为人们居住的宜人便利的地方","ex":{"en":"She now works in urban planning.","cn":"她现在在做城市规划工作。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"计划；规划；设计","en":"Planning is the process of deciding in detail how to do something before you actually start to do it.","ex":{"en":"The trip needs careful planning","cn":"这趟行程需要周密计划。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"城镇规划","en":"Planning is control by the local government of the way that land is used in an area and of what new buildings are built there.","ex":{"en":"...a masterpiece of 18th-century town planning","cn":"18世纪城镇规划的杰作"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"financial planning","cn":"财政计划"}],"base":"plan"},"plethora":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plethora__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plethora__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleθərə","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an amount that is greater than is needed or can be used","cn":"过多；过量；过剩","ex":{"en":"The report contained a plethora of detail.","cn":"报告中细节过多。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"大量；（尤指）过多，过剩","en":"A plethora of something is a large amount of it, especially an amount of it that is greater than you need, want, or can cope with.","ex":{"en":"A plethora of new operators will be allowed to enter the market.","cn":"大批新的运营商将获准进入该市场。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a plethora of suggestions","cn":"一大堆建议"}]},"plus":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plus__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plus__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"plʌs","pos":"preposition","senses":[{"en":"used when the two numbers or amounts mentioned are being added together","cn":"加","ex":{"en":"Two plus five is seven.","cn":"二加五等于七。"}},{"en":"as well as something/somebody; and also","cn":"和；也；外加","ex":{"en":"We have to fit five of us plus all our gear in the car.","cn":"我们五人和全部用具都得塞进车里。"}},{"en":"used after a number to show that the real number or amount is more than the one mentioned","cn":"（用于数字后表示实际数量较大）多，余","ex":{"en":"The work will cost £10 000 plus.","cn":"这项工作将耗资万余英镑。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"above zero","cn":"零度以上；零上","ex":{"en":"The temperature is plus four degrees.","cn":"温度为零上四度。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"used to describe an aspect of something that you consider to be a good thing","cn":"优点的；好的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"One of the hotel's plus points is that it is very central.","cn":"那个旅馆的优势之一是它位于市中心。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"slightly higher than the grade A, B, etc.","cn":"加（用于等级后，表示略高）","g":"[not before noun]","ex":{"en":"I got B plus (B+) in the test.","cn":"我考试得了个 B+。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"an advantage; a good thing","cn":"优势；好处；长处","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"Knowledge of French is a plus in her job.","cn":"通晓法文使她在工作中占优势。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the symbol ( + ), used in mathematics","cn":"加号","ex":{"en":"He put a plus instead of a minus.","cn":"他填了个加号而不是减号。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"used to add more information","cn":"而且；此外；况且","ex":{"en":"I've got too much on at work. Plus my father is not well.","cn":"我工作负担太重了，而且我父亲身体也不好。"},"pos":"conjunction"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"CONJ-COORD 连词","cn":"加；加上","en":"You say plus to show that one number or quantity is being added to another.","ex":{"en":"Send a cheque for £18.99 plus £2 for postage and packing","cn":"请寄上18.99英镑的支票，外加2英镑的邮资和包装费。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"正（数）的；在零以上的","en":"Plus before a number or quantity means that the number or quantity is greater than zero. plus or minus→see: ;","ex":{"en":"The aircraft was subjected to temperatures of minus 65 degrees and plus 120 degrees.","cn":"这架飞机经历了零下65度和零上120度的温度变化。"}},{"pos":"CONJ-COORD 连词","cn":"而且；还有","en":"You can use plus when mentioning an additional item or fact.","ex":{"en":"There's easily enough room for two adults and three children, plus a dog in the boot","cn":"能宽宽松松容下两个大人、三个孩子，而且后备箱里还可以放只狗。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（用于数字或数量后）多于…的","en":"You use plus after a number or quantity to indicate that the actual number or quantity is greater than the one mentioned.","ex":{"en":"There are only 35 staff to serve 30,000-plus customers","cn":"只有35名员工，却要为3万多顾客服务。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"（用于给学生作业评分）好于…的，高于…的","en":"Teachers use plus in grading work in schools and colleges. 'B plus' is a better grade than 'B', but it is not as good as 'A'."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"有利因素；好处","en":"A plus is an advantage or benefit.","ex":{"en":"Experience of any career in sales is a big plus","cn":"任何销售领域的工作经验都是一大优势。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The cost is £22, plus £1 for postage.","cn":"费用为 22 英镑，另加 1 英镑的邮费。"},{"en":"I've got too much on at work. Plus my father is not well.","cn":"我工作负担太重了，而且我父亲身体也不好。"}]},"pleasantly":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplezntli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that is fun, attractive or gives pleasure","cn":"愉快地：以一种有趣，有吸引力或令人愉悦的方式","ex":{"en":"a pleasantly cool room","cn":"凉爽宜人的房间"}},{"en":"in a friendly and polite way","cn":"友好的；和善的；文雅的","ex":{"en":"‘Can I help you?’ he asked pleasantly.","cn":"“需要帮忙吗？”他和颜悦色地问。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/pleasantly__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/pleasantly__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"I was pleasantly surprised by my exam results.","cn":"我的考试成绩真让我喜出望外。"},{"en":"‘Can I help you?’ he asked pleasantly. “","cn":"需要帮忙吗？”他和悦地问道。"}]},"play":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/play__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/play__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pleɪ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to do things for pleasure, as children do; to enjoy yourself, rather than work","cn":"玩耍；游戏；玩乐","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"of children","ex":{"en":"You'll have to play inside today.","cn":"你今天只能在屋里玩耍。"}},{"en":"to pretend to be or do something for fun","cn":"（为玩耍）假装，假扮","g":"[transitive, no passive, intransitive]","sc":"of children","ex":{"en":"Let's play pirates.","cn":"咱们假扮海盗玩吧。"}},{"en":"to be involved in a game; to compete against somebody in a game","cn":"参加比赛；（同某人）比赛","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"sports/games","ex":{"en":"to play football/cards","cn":"踢足球；打牌"}},{"en":"to take a particular position in a sports team","cn":"（在运动队中）担当，充任","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"sports/games","ex":{"en":"Who's playing on the wing?","cn":"谁担任边锋？"}},{"en":"to include somebody in a sports team","cn":"派…出场；让…加入运动队","g":"[transitive]","sc":"sports/games","ex":{"en":"I think we should play Matt on the wing.","cn":"我认为我们应该让麦特打边锋。"}},{"en":"to make contact with the ball and hit or kick it in the way mentioned","cn":"触，带，踢，击（球）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"sports/games","ex":{"en":"She played the ball and ran forward.","cn":"她带球向前冲。"}},{"en":"to move a piece in chess, etc.","cn":"走（子）；行（棋）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"sports/games","ex":{"en":"She played her bishop.","cn":"她走象。"}},{"en":"to put a card face upwards on the table, showing its value","cn":"出牌","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"sports/games","ex":{"en":"to play your ace/a trump","cn":"出 A／王牌"}},{"en":"to perform music on a musical instrument","cn":"演奏（乐曲）","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"music","ex":{"en":"She played Mozart's Piano Concerto No. 20.","cn":"她演奏了莫扎特第 20 钢琴协奏曲。"}},{"en":"to have the skill of performing on a musical instrument","cn":"会演奏，会弹奏（乐器）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"music","ex":{"en":"Do you play a musical instrument?","cn":"你会乐器吗？"}},{"en":"to use an MP3 player, a CD player, etc. to make it possible to hear a song, an album, a CD, etc.","cn":"播放","g":"[transitive]","sc":"music","ex":{"en":"I played some music to drown out the noise.","cn":"我播放音乐来盖过噪声。"}},{"en":"(of a song, an album, etc.) to be heard","cn":"（歌曲、专辑等）被播放","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"music","ex":{"en":"My favourite song was playing on the radio.","cn":"收音机里播放着我最喜爱的歌曲。"}},{"en":"to start working; to make a video or DVD start working","cn":"播放","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"video/DVD","ex":{"en":"These videos won't play on my computer.","cn":"这些视频在我的电脑上不能播放。"}},{"en":"to act in a play, film, etc.; to act the role of somebody","cn":"（在戏剧、电影等中）表演，扮演","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"act/perform","ex":{"en":"to play a role/part","cn":"扮演一个角色"}},{"en":"to pretend to be something that you are not","cn":"佯装；假装","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"act/perform","ex":{"en":"The children were dressed as soldiers, but they were just playing.","cn":"孩子们扮成士兵，但他们只是在装着玩。"}},{"en":"to behave as though you are a particular type of person","cn":"装作；充当","g":"[transitive]","sc":"act/perform","ex":{"en":"This is no time to play the hero.","cn":"这不是充英雄的时候。"}},{"en":"to be performed","cn":"上演；演出","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"act/perform","ex":{"en":"A production of ‘Carmen’ was playing to packed houses.","cn":"《卡门》一剧上演场场爆满。"}},{"en":"to give a performance in a particular place","cn":"在（某地）演出","g":"[transitive]","sc":"act/perform","ex":{"en":"The band are playing 11 cities around the country.","cn":"乐队正在全国 11 个城市巡演。"}},{"en":"to have an effect or influence on something","cn":"（在…中）发挥作用；（对…）产生影响","g":"[transitive]","sc":"have effect","ex":{"en":"Social media played an important part in the last election.","cn":"社交媒体在上一次选举中发挥了重要作用。"}},{"en":"to trick somebody for fun","cn":"捉弄；戏弄","g":"[transitive]","sc":"trick","ex":{"en":"Children ran around the village playing tricks.","cn":"孩子们在村子里跑来跑去捉弄人。"}},{"en":"to deal with a situation in the way mentioned","cn":"（以某种方式）应付，处理","g":"[transitive]","sc":"situation","ex":{"en":"He played the situation carefully for maximum advantage.","cn":"他谨慎应付局面以获得最大利益。"}},{"en":"to do something without being serious about it or putting much effort into it","cn":"敷衍应付；虚与委蛇","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"often disapproving","sc":"not do something seriously","ex":{"en":"He was just playing at it before—now he's serious.","cn":"以前他只是敷衍应付，现在他认真了。"}},{"en":"to be willing to work with other people in a helpful way, especially so that somebody can get what they want","cn":"愿意配合；愿意合作","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"informal","sc":"be willing to help","ex":{"en":"He needs another loan, but the bank won't play.","cn":"他还需要一笔贷款，但银行不配合。"}},{"en":"to move or appear quickly and lightly, often changing direction or shape","cn":"闪烁；浮现；掠过","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of light/a smile","ex":{"en":"Sunlight played on the surface of the lake.","cn":"阳光在湖面上闪烁。"}},{"en":"when a fountain plays, it produces a steady stream of water","cn":"喷涌；涌流","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of fountain","ex":{"en":"Two huge fountains were playing outside the entrance.","cn":"入口处有两个巨大的喷泉正在演奏。"}},{"en":"a piece of writing performed by actors in a theatre or on television or radio","cn":"戏剧；剧本","g":"[countable]","sc":"in theatre","ex":{"en":"a stage/radio play","cn":"舞台剧；广播剧"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"things that people, especially children, do for pleasure rather than as work","cn":"游戏；玩耍；娱乐","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"children","ex":{"en":"the importance of learning through play","cn":"寓教于乐的重要性"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the playing of a game","cn":"比赛；赛风；比赛中的表现","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"Rain stopped play.","cn":"因雨停赛。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"an action or move in a game","cn":"比赛中的动作","g":"[countable]","lab":"North American English","sc":"in sport","ex":{"en":"He made several nice defensive plays.","cn":"他完成了几次漂亮的防守。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the activity or operation of something; the influence of something on something else","cn":"活动；作用；影响","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"activity/influence","ex":{"en":"the free play of market forces","cn":"市场力量的自由调节作用"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the possibility of free and easy movement","cn":"间隙；活动空间","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"in rope","ex":{"en":"We need more play in the rope.","cn":"我们需要再松一松绳子。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a light, quick movement that keeps changing","cn":"轻快变幻的动作；闪烁；闪现","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"literary","sc":"of light/a smile","ex":{"en":"the play of sunlight on water","cn":"阳光在水面上的闪烁"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"玩；玩耍","en":"When children, animals, or perhaps adults play, they spend time doing enjoyable things, such as using toys and taking part in games.","ex":{"en":"...invite the children round to play","cn":"邀请孩子们来玩"}},{"pos":"V-RECIP 相互动词","cn":"参加（体育活动、比赛等）","en":"When you play a sport, game, or match, you take part in it.","ex":{"en":"While the twins played cards, Francis sat reading","cn":"那对双胞胎玩扑克牌的时候，弗朗西斯坐着看书。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（和…）比赛","en":"When one person or team plays another or plays against them, they compete against them in a sport or game.","ex":{"en":"Northern Ireland will play Latvia","cn":"北爱尔兰队将对阵拉脱维亚队。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（比赛等中）打出，踢出，击出（球）","en":"When you play the ball or play a shot in a game or sport, you kick or hit the ball.","ex":{"en":"Think first before playing the ball","cn":"踢出球前先想一想。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"开（玩笑）；耍（花招）；搞（恶作剧）","en":"If you play a joke or a trick on someone, you deceive them or give them a surprise in a way that you think is funny, but that often causes problems for them or annoys them.","ex":{"en":"Someone had played a trick on her, stretched a piece of string at the top of those steps","cn":"有人搞恶作剧整她，在最高的台阶上拉了一根绳子。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"随意摆弄；弄着玩","en":"If you play with an object or with your hair, you keep moving it or touching it with your fingers, perhaps because you are bored or nervous.","ex":{"en":"She stared at the floor, idly playing with the strap of her handbag.","cn":"她眼睛盯着地板，漫不经心地摆弄着手提包的带子。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"剧本；戏剧","en":"A play is a piece of writing which is performed in a theatre, on the radio, or on television.","ex":{"en":"The company put on a play about the homeless","cn":"这家剧团上演了一出讲述无家可归者的戏。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"扮演，饰演（角色等）","en":"If an actor plays a role or character in a play or film, he or she performs the part of that character.","ex":{"en":"...Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde, in which he played Hyde","cn":"他在其中饰演海德一角的《化身博士》"}},{"pos":"V-LINK 连系动词","cn":"装扮；假装；充当","en":"You can use play to describe how someone behaves, when they are deliberately behaving in a certain way or like a certain type of person. For example, to play the innocent, means to pretend to be innocent, and to play deaf means to pretend not to hear something.","ex":{"en":"Hill tried to play the peacemaker","cn":"希尔想要充当和事佬。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（以…方式）对待，处置，处理","en":"You can describe how someone deals with a situation by saying that they play it in a certain way. For example, if someone plays it cool, they keep calm and do not show much emotion, and if someone plays it straight, they behave in an honest and direct way.","ex":{"en":"Investors are playing it cautious, and they're playing it smart.","cn":"投资者审慎精明地行事。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"演奏（乐器或乐曲）","en":"If you play a musical instrument or play a tune on a musical instrument, or if a musical instrument plays, music is produced from it.","ex":{"en":"Nina had been playing the piano","cn":"尼娜一直都在弹钢琴。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"播放（唱片、CD或磁带）","en":"If you play a record, a CD, or a tape, you put it into a machine and sound is produced. If a record, CD, or tape is playing, sound is being produced from it.","ex":{"en":"She played her records too loudly","cn":"她播放唱片时音量太大了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（音乐家、乐队等）表演；举办（音乐会）","en":"If a musician or group of musicians plays or plays a concert, they perform music for people to listen or dance to.","ex":{"en":"A band was playing","cn":"乐队在表演。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（光）轻快地移动","en":"When light plays somewhere, it moves about on a surface in an unsteady way.","ex":{"en":"The sun played on the frosty roofs.","cn":"阳光在结霜的屋顶上闪烁变幻。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"搞什么名堂；干什么蠢事","en":"If you ask what someone is playing at, you are angry because you think they are doing something stupid or wrong.","ex":{"en":"What the hell are you playing at?","cn":"你究竟在搞什么名堂？"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（使）开始活动；（使）投入使用； （使）开始起作用","en":"When something comes into play or is brought into play, it begins to be used or to have an effect.","ex":{"en":"The real existence of a military option will come into play","cn":"存在选择军事手段的切实可能这一点将会起到作用。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（在…中）发挥作用，产生影响","en":"If something or someone plays a part or plays a role in a situation, they are involved in it and have an effect on it.","ex":{"en":"They played a part in the life of their community","cn":"他们参与到了自己社区的生活中。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to play ball→see: ; to play your cards right→see: ; to play it by ear→see: ; to play fair→see: ; to play fast and loose→see: ; to play second fiddle→see: ; to play the field→see: ; to play with fire→see: ; to play the fool→see: ; to play to the gallery→see: ; to play into someone's hands→see: ; to play hard to get→see: ; to play havoc→see: ; to play host→see: ; to play safe→see: ; to play for time→see: ; to play truant→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：play along play around play at play back play down play off against play on play out play up play upon"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The part of Elizabeth was played by Cate Blanchett.","cn":"伊丽莎白这一角色由凯特 · 布兰切特扮演。"},{"en":"She played her two rivals off against each other and got the job herself.","cn":"她挑拨两个对手相争，使自己弄到了那份工作。"}]},"please":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/please__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/please__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pliːz","pos":"exclamation","senses":[{"en":"used as a polite way of asking for something or telling somebody to do something","cn":"（用于客气地请求或吩咐）请，请问","ex":{"en":"Please sit down.","cn":"请坐。"}},{"en":"used to add force to a request or statement","cn":"（用于加强请求或陈述的语气）请千万，请务必，的确","ex":{"en":"Please don't leave me here alone.","cn":"请千万别把我一个人留在这儿。"}},{"en":"used as a polite way of accepting something","cn":"（表示接受的客气话）太感谢了，太好了","ex":{"en":"‘Would you like some help?’ ‘Yes, please.’","cn":"“您需要帮忙吗？”“是的。太感谢了。”"}},{"en":"used to ask somebody to stop behaving badly","cn":"（用于让别人停止不规矩行为）别闹了，行行好","lab":"informal, often humorous，，","ex":{"en":"Children, please! I'm trying to work.","cn":"孩子们，别闹了！我在干活呢。"}},{"en":"used when you are replying to somebody who has said something that you think is stupid","cn":"（认为对方说话荒唐时用）得了吧，算了吧","ex":{"en":"Oh, please! You cannot be serious.","cn":"喔，得了吧！你准是在打哈哈。"}},{"en":"to make somebody happy","cn":"使满意；使愉快","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","ex":{"en":"You can't please everybody.","cn":"你无法让每个人都满意。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"often used after as or what, where, etc. to mean ‘to want’, ‘to choose’ or ‘to like’ to do something","cn":"（常用在 as 或 what、where 等词后）想，选择，喜欢","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"You may stay as long as you please.","cn":"你想待多久就待多久。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"（表示有礼貌地请求或邀请）请，烦劳","en":"You say please when you are politely asking or inviting someone to do something.","ex":{"en":"Can you help us please?","cn":"能请你帮帮我们吗？"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"（表示客气地接受）谢谢，行","en":"You say please when you are accepting something politely.","ex":{"en":"'Tea?' — 'Yes, please.'","cn":"“要茶吗？”——“好的，谢谢。”"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（表示要求对方停止做某事或别再开口）请别，请不必","en":"You can say please to indicate that you want someone to stop doing something or stop speaking. You would say this if, for example, what they are doing or saying makes you angry or upset.","ex":{"en":"Please, Mary, this is all so unnecessary","cn":"玛丽，请不要这样，这完全没必要。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（用于吸引对方注意、特别是儿童对老师或其他成人时）请问，对不起","en":"You can say please in order to attract someone's attention politely. Children in particular say 'please ' to attract the attention of a teacher or other adult.","ex":{"en":"Please sir, can we have some more?","cn":"请问，先生，我们能再要一些吗？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使高兴；使喜欢；使满意","en":"If someone or something pleases you, they make you feel happy and satisfied.","ex":{"en":"More than anything, I want to please you","cn":"最重要的是，我想让你高兴。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"愿意；喜欢；认为合适","en":"You use please in expressions such as as she pleases ,whatever you please, and anything he pleases to indicate that someone can do or have whatever they want.","ex":{"en":"Women should be free to dress and act as they please","cn":"女性应该有穿衣和行动的自由。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（用于强调）极尽…，…的程度怎么说都不为过","en":"You can use as you please in expressions such as bold as you please or casually as you please or charming as you please in order to emphasize what you are saying.","ex":{"en":"He walked by my table and, casually as you please, picked up my address book","cn":"他走到我的桌旁，非常随意地拿起了我的通讯录。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（表示很有礼貌和正式地吸引对方注意或提出请求）对不起，烦请","en":"If you please is sometimes used as a very polite and formal way of attracting someone's attention or of asking them to do something.","ex":{"en":"Ladies and gentlemen, if you please. Miss Taylor's going to play for us","cn":"女士们，先生们，烦请泰勒小姐为我们表演。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（表示惊讶、恼怒或难以置信）竟然，你说怪不怪","en":"You can say if you please to indicate that a situation surprises or annoys you, or is difficult to believe.","ex":{"en":"She was pretty unforthcoming. Made Sally wait till she'd cooked Selby's lunch, if you please.","cn":"她爱搭不理地把萨莉晾在一边，直到她为塞尔比做好午饭，你说怪不怪。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（无礼地表示不在意或不关心）请便，随你的便","en":"You say 'please yourself ' to indicate in a rather rude way that you do not mind or care whether the person you are talking to does a particular thing or not.","ex":{"en":"'Do you mind if I wait?' I asked. Melanie shrugged: 'Please yourself.'","cn":"我问道：“要不我等会儿吧？”梅拉妮耸耸肩说：“随你便。”"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"please God→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘I don't think I'll bother finishing this.’ ‘Please yourself.’ “","cn":"我想我不会费力做完这件事。” “随你的便。”"},{"en":"‘Would you like some help?’ ‘Yes, please.’ “","cn":"您需要帮忙吗？” “是的。太感谢了。”"}]},"placid":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/placid__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/placid__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplæsɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not easily excited or annoyed","cn":"温和的；温顺的；文静的","ex":{"en":"a placid baby/horse","cn":"安静的婴儿；驯良的马"}},{"en":"calm and peaceful, with very little movement","cn":"平静的；宁静的；安静的","ex":{"en":"the placid waters of the lake","cn":"平静的湖水"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"平和的；温和的","en":"A placid person or animal is calm and does not easily become excited, angry, or upset.","ex":{"en":"She was a placid child who rarely cried","cn":"她是个性情温和的孩子，很少哭闹。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"宁静的；平静的；安宁的","en":"A placid place, area of water, or life is calm and peaceful.","ex":{"en":"...the placid waters of Lake Erie","cn":"伊利湖宁静的湖水"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"the placid waters of the lake","cn":"平静的湖水"},{"en":"a placid baby/horse","cn":"安静的婴儿；驯良的马"}]},"placeholders":{"lemma":"placeholder","media":{"uk":"media/uk/placeholder__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/placeholder__us_1.mp3"}},"platform":{"media":{"img":["media/pic/shoes_comp.jpg","media/thumb/platform.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/platform__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/platform__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplætfɔːm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the raised flat area next to the track at a train station where you get on or off the train","cn":"站台；月台","lab":"British English","sc":"at train station","ex":{"en":"What platform does it go from?","cn":"火车从哪个站台发车？"}},{"en":"a flat surface raised above the level of the ground or floor, used by public speakers or performers so that the audience can see them","cn":"讲台；舞台","sc":"for performers","ex":{"en":"Coming onto the platform now is tonight's conductor, Jane Glover.","cn":"现在出场的是今晚的指挥简·格洛弗。"}},{"en":"a raised level surface, for example one that equipment stands on or is operated from","cn":"平台","sc":"raised surface","ex":{"en":"an oil/gas platform","cn":"石油／天然气钻井平台"}},{"en":"the type of computer system or the software that is used","cn":"计算机平台","sc":"computing","ex":{"en":"a multimedia platform","cn":"多媒体平台"}},{"en":"the aims of a political party and the things that they say they will do if they are elected to power","cn":"（政党的）纲领，政纲，宣言","g":"[usually singular]","sc":"politics/opinions","ex":{"en":"They are campaigning on an anti-immigration platform.","cn":"他们正在宣传反对外来移民的政纲。"}},{"en":"an opportunity or a place for somebody to express their opinions publicly or make progress in a particular area","cn":"（公开表达意见或在某方面发展的）机会，阵地，讲坛","sc":"politics/opinions","ex":{"en":"She used the newspaper column as a platform for her feminist views.","cn":"她以这个报纸专栏为讲坛，宣传她的女权主义观点。"}},{"en":"a type of shoe with a high, thick sole; the sole on such a shoe","cn":"厚底鞋；厚鞋底","sc":"shoes","ex":{"en":"platform shoes","cn":"厚底鞋"}},{"en":"the open part at the back of a double-decker bus where you get on or off","cn":"（双层汽车的）上下车出入口，入口平台","lab":"British English","sc":"on bus"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（通常为木制的）讲台，舞台","en":"A platform is a flat, raised structure, usually made of wood, which people stand on when they make speeches or give a performance.","ex":{"en":"Nick finished what he was saying and jumped down from the platform.","cn":"尼克讲完后，从讲台上跳了下来。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（通常作为架放或着陆用的）平台","en":"A platform is a flat raised structure or area, usually one which something can stand on or land on.","ex":{"en":"Some of these flood shelters are on raised platforms, which have allowed government helicopters to land amid the continuing floods","cn":"其中一些防洪棚搭建在高台上，高台可供政府的直升机在持续的洪水中降落。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（海上）钻井平台","en":"A platform is a structure built for people to work and live on when drilling for oil or gas at sea, or when extracting it."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（火车站的）站台，月台","en":"A platform in a railway station is the area beside the rails where you wait for or get off a train.","ex":{"en":"The train was about to leave and I was not even on the platform.","cn":"火车就快开了，可我还没到站台。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（政党的）纲领，政纲，宣言","en":"The platform of a political party is what they say they will do if they are elected.","ex":{"en":"...a platform of political and economic reforms","cn":"政治和经济改革纲领"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（公开发表意见或表达愿望的）机会，论坛","en":"If someone has a platform, they have an opportunity to tell people what they think or want.","ex":{"en":"The demonstration provided a platform for a broad cross section of speakers.","cn":"示威集会为具有广泛代表性的人士提供了发表意见的机会。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"（公共汽车上供乘客上下车的）踏脚台","en":"In a bus, the platform is the area of floor at the front or back where you get on and off.","ex":{"en":"I stood on the crowded back platform of the seven o'clock bus as it lurched along the wet damp street.","cn":"我站在早晨7点那班公共汽车拥挤的后门处，随着它沿潮湿的街道蹒跚行进。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She used the newspaper column as a platform for her feminist views.","cn":"她以这个报纸专栏为讲坛，宣传她的女权主义观点。"},{"en":"( BrE ) The train now standing at platform 1 is for Leeds.","cn":"停靠在 1 号站台的火车是开往利兹的。"}]},"playing":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/playing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/playing__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the way in which somebody plays something, especially a musical instrument","cn":"（尤指演奏的）表现，风格","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The orchestral playing is superb.","cn":"这个管弦乐团的演奏棒极了。"}},{"en":"the act of playing a piece of music","cn":"（乐曲）演奏","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"repeated playings of the National Anthem","cn":"国歌反复的演奏"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The orchestral playing is superb.","cn":"这个管弦乐团的演奏棒极了。"},{"en":"repeated playings of the National Anthem","cn":"国歌反复的演奏"}],"base":"play"},"placement":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/placement__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/placement__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪsmənt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of finding somebody a suitable job or place to live","cn":"（对人的）安置，安排","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a job placement service","cn":"职业介绍所"}},{"en":"a job, often as part of a course of study, where you get some experience of a particular kind of work","cn":"实习工作；实习课","g":"[countable, uncountable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"The course includes a placement in Year 3.","cn":"本课程第 3 年有实习课。"}},{"en":"the act of placing something somewhere","cn":"（对物件的）安置，放置","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"This procedure ensures correct placement of the catheter.","cn":"这个程序可保证导管的正确置入。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"放置；布置；部署","en":"The placement of something or someone is the act of putting them in a particular place or position.","ex":{"en":"The treatment involves the placement of twenty-two electrodes in the inner ear.","cn":"这一治疗需要在内耳放置22个电极。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（培训中的）实习安排","en":"If someone who is training gets a placement, they get a job for a period of time which is intended to give them experience in the work they are training for.","ex":{"en":"He had a six-month work placement with the Japanese government.","cn":"他被安排在日本政府部门实习了6个月。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（人员的）安插，安置","en":"The placement of someone in a job, home, or school is the act or process of finding them a job, home, or school.","ex":{"en":"The children were waiting for placement in a foster care home","cn":"这些孩子在抚育院等待安置。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"收容所；安置所","en":"You can refer to a home that is found for someone who is unable to look after themselves, for example a child, as a placement .","ex":{"en":"This home seemed like a good placement for Sarah.","cn":"这家养育院对萨拉来说似乎是一个合适的收容之所。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"This procedure ensures correct placement of the catheter.","cn":"这个程序可保证导液管的正确置入。"},{"en":"The third year is spent on placement in selected companies.","cn":"第三年是在选定的公司里实习。"}]},"plush":{"oxford":{"phon":"plʌʃ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a type of silk or cotton cloth with a thick soft surface made of a mass of threads","cn":"（丝或棉的）长毛绒","ex":{"en":"red plush armchairs","cn":"红色长毛绒扶手椅"}},{"en":"very comfortable; expensive and of good quality","cn":"舒适的；豪华的","ex":{"en":"a plush hotel","cn":"豪华的旅馆"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"豪华的；奢华的；舒适的","en":"If you describe something as plush, you mean that it is very smart, comfortable, or expensive.","ex":{"en":"...a plush, four-storey, Georgian house in Mayfair.","cn":"坐落在梅费尔的乔治王朝时期风格的4层豪宅"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（尤用于地毯和给家具覆面的）长毛绒","en":"Plush is a thick soft material like velvet, used especially for carpets and to cover furniture.","ex":{"en":"All the seats were in red plush.","cn":"所有座位都上了红色长毛绒面。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plush__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plush__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"red plush armchairs","cn":"红色长毛绒扶手椅"},{"en":"a plush hotel","cn":"豪华的旅馆"}]},"plume":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plume__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plume__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pluːm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a cloud of something that rises and curves upwards in the air","cn":"飘升之物","ex":{"en":"a plume of smoke","cn":"一缕青烟"}},{"en":"a large feather","cn":"翎；羽毛","ex":{"en":"a black hat with an ostrich plume","cn":"饰有一根鸵鸟羽毛的黑帽子"}},{"en":"a group of feathers or long thin pieces of material tied together and often used as a decoration","cn":"（常用作饰物的）连在一起的羽毛，羽状物；羽饰","ex":{"en":"The red plume on the horse’s head was nodding to the rhythm of its steps.","cn":"马头上的红色羽毛随着马蹄的节奏点头。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（尘、火、水等升起的）（一）股，（一）团","en":"A plume of smoke, dust, fire, or water is a large quantity of it that rises into the air in a column.","ex":{"en":"The rising plume of black smoke could be seen all over Kabul.","cn":"整个喀布尔都能看到腾起的黑烟。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"羽毛；大羽","en":"A plume is a large, soft bird's feather.","ex":{"en":"...broad straw hats decorated with ostrich plumes.","cn":"装饰着鸵鸟羽毛的宽边草帽"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（战士头盔等的）羽饰","en":"A plume is a bunch of long, thin pieces of material which is used to decorate something such as a soldier's helmet."}]},"examples":[{"en":"a black hat with an ostrich plume","cn":"饰有一根鸵鸟羽毛的黑帽子"},{"en":"a plume of smoke","cn":"一缕青烟"}]},"plainly":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plainly__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plainly__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪnli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that is easy to see, hear, understand or believe","cn":"清晰地；明显地；清楚地","ex":{"en":"The sea was plainly visible in the distance.","cn":"大海在远处清晰可见。"}},{"en":"using simple words to say something in a direct and honest way","cn":"简单明了地；直截了当地","ex":{"en":"He told her plainly that he thought she was making a big mistake.","cn":"他坦白地告诉她，他认为她犯了一个大错误。"}},{"en":"in a simple way, without decoration","cn":"简朴地；朴素地","ex":{"en":"She was plainly dressed and wore no make-up.","cn":"她衣着朴素，粉黛不施。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"显然；显而易见地","en":"You use plainly to indicate that you believe something is obviously true, often when you are trying to convince someone else that it is true.","ex":{"en":"The judge's conclusion was plainly wrong","cn":"法官的结论明摆着是错的。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"明显地；清楚地；清晰地","en":"You use plainly to indicate that something is easily seen, noticed, or recognized.","ex":{"en":"He was plainly annoyed","cn":"他明显是生气了。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"直率地；直截了当地","en":"If you say something plainly, you say it in a direct and honest way, without trying to hide the facts.","ex":{"en":"'You're a coward,' Mark said very plainly and soberly","cn":"马克非常直率而严肃地说：“你是个懦夫。”"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She had no right to interfere in what was plainly a family matter.","cn":"这事明摆着是别人的家事，她无权干涉。"},{"en":"The lease plainly states that all damage must be paid for.","cn":"租约明确规定，一切损坏必须赔偿。"}]},"plastics":{"lemma":"plastic","media":{"img":["media/pic/cupsandglasses_diningroom_comp.jpg","media/thumb/plastic.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/plastic__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plastic__us_1.mp3"}},"plot":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plot__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plot__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"plɒt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the series of events that form the story of a novel, play, film, etc.","cn":"故事情节；布局","g":"[countable, uncountable]","lab":"US English","ex":{"en":"It's hard to follow the plot of the film.","cn":"很难跟上电影的情节。"}},{"en":"a secret plan made by a group of people to do something wrong or illegal","cn":"阴谋；密谋","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"He had been the victim of an elaborate murder plot.","cn":"他是一场精心策划的谋杀阴谋的受害者。"}},{"en":"a small piece of land that is used or intended for a special purpose","cn":"（专用的）小块土地","g":"[countable]","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"She bought a small plot of land to build a house on.","cn":"她买了一小块地盖房子。"}},{"en":"to make a secret plan to harm somebody, especially a government or its leader","cn":"密谋；暗中策划","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"It is claimed he plotted with the country's enemies.","cn":"据称他与该国的敌人密谋。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to mark something on a map, for example the position or course of something","cn":"（在地图上）画出，标出","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"The earthquake centres had been plotted on a world map.","cn":"地震震中均被标示在一张世界地图上。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make a diagram or chart from some information","cn":"绘制（图表）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"We carefully plotted each patient's response to the drug on a chart.","cn":"我们仔细绘出了每个病人对这种药物反应的图表。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to mark points on a graph and draw a line or curve connecting them","cn":"绘制（图表的曲线）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"First, plot the temperature curve on the graph.","cn":"首先，在图表上绘出温度曲线来。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to write the plot of a novel, play, etc.","cn":"（为小说、戏剧等）设计情节，布局","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"a tightly-plotted thriller","cn":"情节丝丝入扣的惊险刺激小说"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"阴谋；密谋","en":"A plot is a secret plan by a group of people to do something that is illegal or wrong, usually against a person or a government.","ex":{"en":"Security forces have uncovered a plot to overthrow the government","cn":"安全部队揭露了一起推翻政府的阴谋。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"图谋；密谋","en":"If people plot to do something or plot something that is illegal or wrong, they plan secretly to do it.","ex":{"en":"Prosecutors in the trial allege the defendants plotted to overthrow the government","cn":"检方在审判中指称被告密谋推翻政府。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"计划；制订","en":"When people plot a strategy or a course of action, they carefully plan each step of it.","ex":{"en":"Yesterday's meeting was intended to plot a survival strategy for the party","cn":"昨天的会议旨在制订使该党能够继续存在下去的策略。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（电影、小说或戏剧的）情节","en":"The plot of a film, novel, or play is the connected series of events which make up the story."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（尤指作特殊用途的）一小块（土地）","en":"A plot of land is a small piece of land, especially one that has been measured or marked out for a special purpose, such as building houses or growing vegetables.","ex":{"en":"I thought that I'd buy myself a small plot of land and build a house on it","cn":"我想我该给自己买一小块地，在上面建一座房子。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"绘制…的曲线","en":"When someone plots something on a graph, they mark certain points on it and then join the points up.","ex":{"en":"We plot about eight points on the graph.","cn":"我们在图表上绘制出大约8个点的曲线。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（在地图上）标绘出（飞机、船舶的位置或航线）","en":"When someone plots the position or course of a plane or ship, they mark it on a map using instruments to obtain accurate information.","ex":{"en":"We were trying to plot the course of the submarine.","cn":"我们试图标绘出潜艇的航线图。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"绘制…的图表（或平面图）","en":"If someone plots the progress or development of something, they make a diagram or a plan which shows how it has developed in order to give some indication of how it will develop in the future.","ex":{"en":"They used a computer to plot the movements of everyone in the building.","cn":"他们使用了一台计算机绘制这座建筑里每个人的活动图表。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"困惑；迷惘；不知所措","en":"If someone loses the plot, they become confused and do not know what they should do.","ex":{"en":"The Tories have lost the plot on law and order.","cn":"保守党人在治安问题上不知所措。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"We carefully plotted each patient's response to the drug on a chart.","cn":"我们仔细绘出了每个病人对这种药物反应的图表。"},{"en":"The earthquake centres had been plotted on a world map.","cn":"地震震中均被标示在一张世界地图上。"}]},"playful":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/playful__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/playful__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪfl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"full of fun; wanting to play","cn":"有趣的；爱嬉戏的；爱玩的","ex":{"en":"a playful puppy","cn":"顽皮的小狗"}},{"en":"made or done in fun; not serious","cn":"打趣的；闹着玩的；嬉戏的","ex":{"en":"He gave her a playful punch on the arm.","cn":"他开玩笑地捶了一下她的胳膊。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（姿态或人）嬉戏的，闹着玩的，不当真的","en":"A playful gesture or person is friendly or humorous.","ex":{"en":"...a playful kiss on the tip of his nose.","cn":"在他鼻尖上的戏吻"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（动物）喜玩耍的，活泼的","en":"A playful animal is lively and cheerful.","ex":{"en":"...a playful puppy.","cn":"顽皮的小狗"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He gave her a playful punch on the arm.","cn":"他开玩笑地捶了一下她的胳膊。"},{"en":"a playful puppy","cn":"顽皮的小狗"}]},"playground":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪɡraʊnd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an outdoor area where children can play, especially at a school or in a park","cn":"（尤指学校的）操场；（尤指公园中的）游戏场，游乐场","ex":{"en":"a school playground","cn":"操场"}},{"en":"a place where a particular type of people go to enjoy themselves","cn":"（某些集体聚会游乐的）园地，天地，活动场所","ex":{"en":"The resort is a playground of the rich and famous.","cn":"这个度假胜地是富翁名流的娱乐场所。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（学校的）操场，运动场；（儿童）游乐场","en":"A playground is a piece of land, at school or in a public area, where children can play."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（某一群体的）游憩胜地，度假场所","en":"If you describe a place as a playground for a certain group of people, you mean that those people like to enjoy themselves there or go on holiday there.","ex":{"en":"...St Tropez, playground of the rich and famous.","cn":"圣特罗佩，富豪和名流的游憩胜地"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/playground__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/playground__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The resort is a playground of the rich and famous.","cn":"这个度假胜地是富翁名流的娱乐场所。"},{"en":"children shouting and running in the playground","cn":"在操场上叫嚷奔跑的孩子们"}]},"plug":{"oxford":{"phon":"plʌɡ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to fill a hole with a substance or piece of material that fits tightly into it","cn":"堵塞；封堵","sc":"fill hole","ex":{"en":"He plugged the hole in the pipe with an old rag.","cn":"他用一块旧破布把管子上的那个洞塞住了。"}},{"en":"to provide something that has been missing from a particular situation and is needed in order to improve it","cn":"补足；补充；供给","sc":"provide something missing","ex":{"en":"A cheaper range of products was introduced to plug the gap at the lower end of the market.","cn":"推出相对廉价的一系列产品是为了填补较低端市场的缺口。"}},{"en":"to give praise or attention to a new book, film, etc. in order to encourage people to buy it or see it","cn":"推广；宣传","lab":"informal","sc":"book/movie","ex":{"en":"She came on the show to plug her latest album.","cn":"她上电视节目宣传她的新唱片专辑。"}},{"en":"to shoot somebody","cn":"射击；射杀","lab":"North American English, old-fashioned, informal，，，，","sc":"shoot"},{"en":"a small plastic object with two or three metal pins that connects a piece of electrical equipment to the main supply of electricity","cn":"插头","sc":"electrical equipment","ex":{"en":"The iron is fitted with a three-pin plug.","cn":"熨斗配有三脚插头。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a small opening in a wall, by which you connect a piece of electrical equipment to the main supply of electricity","cn":"（电源）插座","lab":"informal, especially British English，，","sc":"electrical equipment","ex":{"en":"Can I use this plug for my iron?","cn":"我能用这个插座插熨斗吗？"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a small object that connects a wire from one piece of electrical equipment to an opening in another","cn":"转换插头","sc":"electrical equipment","ex":{"en":"the plug from the computer to the printer","cn":"连接电脑和打印机的转换插头"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a part in a car engine that produces a spark (= a flash of electricity) which makes the fuel burn and starts the engine","cn":"火花塞","lab":"British English also","sc":"in engine","pos":"noun"},{"en":"a thick round piece of plastic, rubber or metal that you put in the hole in a bath or a sink to stop the water flowing out","cn":"塞子","sc":"in bath/sink","ex":{"en":"She pulled out the plug and let the water drain away.","cn":"她拔起塞子放掉了水。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a round piece of material that fits into a hole and blocks it","cn":"堵塞物；塞子","sc":"in hole","ex":{"en":"She took the plug of cotton wool from her ear.","cn":"她从耳朵中取出棉毛耳塞来。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"an object that fits into the top of a bottle to close it","cn":"瓶塞","lab":"North American English","sc":"in hole","pos":"noun"},{"en":"a small plastic tube that you put into a hole in a wall so that it will hold a screw","cn":"螺钉楔子，螺钉塞栓（塞入洞中用来固定螺丝的小塑料管）","sc":"for screw","pos":"noun"},{"en":"praise or attention that somebody gives to a new book, film, etc. in order to encourage people to buy or see it","cn":"推销；宣传","lab":"informal","sc":"for book/movie","ex":{"en":"He managed to get in a plug for his new book.","cn":"他设法为自己的新书插入了一条宣传信息。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"插头","en":"A plug on a piece of electrical equipment is a small plastic object with two or three metal pins which fit into the holes of an electric socket and connects the equipment to the electricity supply."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"插座","en":"A plug is an electric socket."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（浴缸或水槽的）塞子","en":"A plug is a thick, circular piece of rubber or plastic that you use to block the hole in a bath or sink when it is filled with water.","ex":{"en":"She put the plug in the sink and filled it with cold water.","cn":"她把水槽的塞子塞上，注满凉水。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（木头、塑料或蜡制的堵洞）塞子，栓","en":"A plug is a small, round piece of wood, plastic, or wax which is used to block holes.","ex":{"en":"A plug had been inserted in the drill hole.","cn":"钻孔已塞上了塞子。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"把…塞住；堵塞；填塞","en":"If you plug a hole, you block it with something.","ex":{"en":"Crews are working to plug a major oil leak.","cn":"船员正在封堵一个漏油的大洞。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"大肆宣传（尤指书或电影）；为…大做广告","en":"If someone plugs a commercial product, especially a book or a film, they praise it in order to encourage people to buy it or see it because they have an interest in it doing well.","ex":{"en":"We did not want people on the show who are purely interested in plugging a book or film.","cn":"我们不想让那些只想为书或电影做广告的人上节目。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"停止；中断；取消","en":"If someone in a position of power pulls the plug on a project or on someone's activities, they use their power to stop them continuing.","ex":{"en":"The banks have the power to pull the plug on the project.","cn":"银行能让该工程下马。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：plug away plug in plug into"}]},"media":{"img":["media/pic/plug_comp.jpg","media/thumb/plug.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/plug__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plug__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"A cheaper range of products was introduced to plug the gap at the lower end of the market.","cn":"推出相对廉价的一系列产品是为了填补较低端市场的缺口。"},{"en":"The company has doubled its profits since plugging into lucrative overseas markets.","cn":"自从这家公司进入赚钱的海外市场以后，利润翻了一番。"}]},"plain":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plain__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plain__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pleɪn","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not decorated or complicated; simple","cn":"不尚修饰的；朴素的；简单的","ex":{"en":"a plain but elegant dress","cn":"朴素淡雅的连衣裙"}},{"en":"without marks or a pattern on it","cn":"素的；无花纹的；单色的","ex":{"en":"covers in plain or printed cotton","cn":"单色或印花的罩布"}},{"en":"easy to see or understand","cn":"清楚的；明显的；浅白的","ex":{"en":"He made it plain that we should leave.","cn":"他明确表示要我们离开。"}},{"en":"not trying to trick anyone; honest and direct","cn":"坦诚的；直率的；直接的","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"The plain fact is that nobody really knows.","cn":"事实很明显，没有人真正了解。"}},{"en":"used to emphasize that something is very ordinary, not special in any way","cn":"极普通的；平庸的；平凡的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"You don't need any special skills for this job, just plain common sense.","cn":"这项工作不需要任何特殊技能，只要有普通常识就够了。"}},{"en":"not beautiful or attractive","cn":"相貌平平的；无姿色的","ex":{"en":"She looked very plain and dowdy.","cn":"她长得非常普通，衣也过时。"}},{"en":"describing a simple stitch used in knitting","cn":"（编织）平针的，平纹的"},{"en":"a large area of flat land","cn":"平原","ex":{"en":"the flat coastal plain of Thassos","cn":"萨索斯岛平坦的滨海平原"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"used to emphasize how bad, stupid, etc. something is","cn":"（用于强调）简直，绝对","ex":{"en":"plain stupid/wrong","cn":"简直愚蠢至极；绝对错误"},"pos":"adverb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"单色的；素色的；无花纹（或图案、字迹）的","en":"A plain object, surface, or fabric is entirely in one colour and has no pattern, design, or writing on it.","ex":{"en":"In general, a plain carpet makes a room look bigger","cn":"一般来说，单色的地毯使房间显得更宽敞。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"朴素的；简朴的","en":"Something that is plain is very simple in style.","ex":{"en":"Bronwen's dress was plain but it hung well on her","cn":"布朗温的长裙虽然朴素，却很合身。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"明显的；明白的；清楚的","en":"If a fact, situation, or statement is plain, it is easy to recognize or understand.","ex":{"en":"It was plain to him that I was having a nervous breakdown","cn":"他能明显地看出我快要精神崩溃了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（相貌）平常的，不好看的","en":"If you describe someone as plain, you think they look ordinary and not at all beautiful.","ex":{"en":"...a shy, rather plain girl with a pale complexion.","cn":"肤色苍白、相貌平平的害羞女孩"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"平原；（几乎没有树木的）大片平地","en":"A plain is a large flat area of land with very few trees on it.","ex":{"en":"Once there were 70 million buffalo on the plains.","cn":"北美大平原上曾有过7,000万头野牛。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"（用于形容词前加强语气）显然，完全地","en":"You can use plain before an adjective in order to emphasize it.","ex":{"en":"The food was just plain terrible.","cn":"这食物实在太难吃了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（尤在与另一个更加不同寻常或让人印象深刻的名字比较时表示强调）普通的，平凡的","en":"You can use plain before a name to emphasize how simple and ordinary it is, especially when you are comparing it with another more unusual or impressive name.","ex":{"en":"Why couldn't they call you plain Ann or Alice like the rest?","cn":"他们为什么不能像其他人一样，给你取个普普通通的安或艾丽斯的名字呢？"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（警察）穿便衣的","en":"If a police officer is in plain clothes, he or she is wearing ordinary clothes instead of a police uniform.","ex":{"en":"Three officers in plain clothes told me to get out of the car.","cn":"3名便衣警察让我下车。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"plain sailing→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"You don't need any special skills for this job, just plain common sense.","cn":"这项工作不需要任何特殊技能，只要有普通常识就够了。"},{"en":"She gave me only the bare facts of the case.","cn":"她只给我介绍了这个案件的一些基本情况。"}]},"plain-clothes":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（警察）穿便衣的","en":"Plain-clothes police officers wear ordinary clothes instead of a police uniform. in plain clothes→see: ;","ex":{"en":"He was arrested by plain-clothes detectives as he walked through the customs hall.","cn":"他穿过海关大厅时被便衣侦探逮捕。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plain_clothes_1_gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plain_clothes_1_us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"plain-clothes police officers","cn":"便衣警察"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌpleɪn ˈkləʊðz","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"ordinary clothes, not uniform, when worn by police officers on duty","cn":"（警察执行任务时穿的）便衣，便服","ex":{"en":"officers in plain clothes","cn":"便衣警察"}},{"en":"wearing ordinary clothes, not uniform","cn":"（警察执行任务时穿的）便衣，便服","ex":{"en":"plain-clothes police officers","cn":"便衣警察"},"pos":"adjective"}]}},"place":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/place__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/place__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pleɪs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a particular position, point or area","cn":"位置；地点；场所；地方","g":"[countable]","sc":"position/point/area","ex":{"en":"Keep your purse in a safe place.","cn":"把钱包放在安全的地方。"}},{"en":"a particular city, town, building, etc.","cn":"某处地方（如城镇或建筑物等）","g":"[countable]","sc":"city/town/building","ex":{"en":"I can't remember all the places we visited in Thailand.","cn":"我记不清在泰国参观过的所有地方。"}},{"en":"a building or an area of land used for a particular purpose","cn":"有某用途的建筑（或土地）","g":"[countable]","lab":"formal","sc":"city/town/building","ex":{"en":"The town has many excellent eating places.","cn":"镇上有许多很棒的餐馆。"}},{"en":"a particular area on a surface, especially on a person’s body","cn":"表面的某处；（尤指）身体某处","g":"[countable]","sc":"area on surface","ex":{"en":"He broke his arm in three places.","cn":"他胳膊上有三处骨折。"}},{"en":"a point in a book, speech, piece of music, etc., especially one that somebody has reached at a particular time","cn":"段；点；节；（尤指）读到的（或说到的）某点","g":"[countable]","sc":"in book/speech, etc.","ex":{"en":"She had marked her place with a bookmark.","cn":"她把书签夹在读到的地方。"}},{"en":"the natural or correct position for something","cn":"恰当位置；适当的地方","g":"[countable]","sc":"correct position","ex":{"en":"Is there a place on the form to put your address?","cn":"表格上有填写地址的位置吗？"}},{"en":"a position, seat, etc., especially one that is available for or being used by a person or vehicle","cn":"（尤指占用或空着的）座位，位置，泊位","g":"[countable]","sc":"seat","ex":{"en":"Come and sit here—I've saved you a place.","cn":"到这儿来坐吧。我给你留了个座位。"}},{"en":"an opportunity to take part in something, especially to study at a school or university or on a course","cn":"求学机会；进修机会；入学名额","g":"[countable]","sc":"at university/school","ex":{"en":"She's been offered a place at Bath to study Business.","cn":"她已被录取到巴斯大学读商科。"}},{"en":"the position of being a member of a sports team","cn":"队员身份；队员资格","g":"[countable]","sc":"in sports team","ex":{"en":"She has won a place in the Olympic team.","cn":"她已获得奥运代表队的队员资格。"}},{"en":"a position among the winners of a race or competition; a position in the next stage of a competition","cn":"（比赛优胜者的）名次；（进入下一阶段比赛的）资格","g":"[countable, usually singular]","sc":"in race/competition","ex":{"en":"She took third place.","cn":"她获得了第三名。"}},{"en":"the role or importance of somebody/something in a particular situation, usually in relation to others","cn":"身份；地位；资格","g":"[singular]","sc":"role/importance","ex":{"en":"He is assured of his place in history.","cn":"他必定会被载入史册。"}},{"en":"a house or flat; a person’s home","cn":"家；住处","g":"[singular]","lab":"informal","sc":"home","ex":{"en":"What about dinner at my place?","cn":"到我家吃晚饭好不好？"}},{"en":"a suitable or safe area for somebody to be","cn":"适当的（或安全的）处所","g":"[countable]","sc":"safe area","ex":{"en":"These streets are no place for a child to be out alone at night.","cn":"这些街道可不是小孩子夜间单独去的地方。"}},{"en":"the position of a figure after a decimal point","cn":"（小数点后的）位","g":"[countable]","sc":"mathematics","ex":{"en":"Convert the decimal to a percentage by moving the decimal point two places to the right.","cn":"通过将小数点向右移动两位，将小数转换为百分比。"}},{"en":"used as part of a name for a short street or square","cn":"（作短街道或广场名称的一部分）","g":"[singular]","sc":"street/square","ex":{"en":"66 Portland Place","cn":"波特兰街 66 号"}},{"en":"to put something in a particular place, especially when you do it carefully or deliberately","cn":"（尤指小心或有意）放置，安放","g":"[transitive]","sc":"in position","ex":{"en":"He placed his hand on her shoulder.","cn":"他把手搭在她的肩上。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"used to express the attitude somebody has towards something/somebody","cn":"以某种态度对待（或看待）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"attitude","ex":{"en":"They place a high value on punctuality.","cn":"他们对守时极为重视。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to give instructions about something or make a request for something to happen","cn":"下指示；请求","g":"[transitive]","sc":"bet/order/advertisement","ex":{"en":"to place an order/a bet","cn":"下订单；下赌注"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to put somebody/yourself in a particular situation","cn":"使（人）处于某位置；安置；安顿","g":"[transitive]","sc":"in situation","ex":{"en":"to place somebody in command","cn":"让某人指挥"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to find a suitable job, home, etc. for somebody","cn":"安顿；安置","g":"[transitive]","sc":"find home/job","ex":{"en":"The agency placed about 2 000 secretaries last year.","cn":"去年，这家中介所为大约 2 000 名秘书找到了工作。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to decide that somebody/something has a particular position or rank compared with other people or things","cn":"（经比较）归类，划分，排名次","g":"[transitive]","sc":"give rank","ex":{"en":"I would place her among the top five tennis players in the world.","cn":"我会把她排在世界五名顶尖网球选手之列。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"used to describe a person, a team, a horse, etc. finishing in a particular position in a race","cn":"排名；获名次","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","lab":"British English","sc":"in race","ex":{"en":"He was placed fifth in last Saturday's race.","cn":"在上周六的径赛中，他名列第五。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to recognize somebody/something and be able to identify them/it","cn":"认出；辨认；识别","g":"[transitive]","sc":"recognize","ex":{"en":"I've seen her before but I just can't place her.","cn":"我从前见过她，不过现在认不出她来。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-IN-NAMES 名称名词","cn":"（用于广场或较短街道的名称中）广场，街","en":"Place is used as part of the name of a square or short street in a town.","ex":{"en":"...15 Portland Place, London W1A 4DD.","cn":"伦敦波特兰街15号，邮编WIA 4DD"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The agency placed about 2 000 secretaries last year.","cn":"去年，这家中介所为大约 2 000 名秘书找到了工作。"},{"en":"I'm fed up with living with my parents, so I'm looking for a place of my own.","cn":"我腻烦跟父母同住了，所以正在找一个属于自己的住处。"}]},"planet":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/planet__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/planet__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/planet.jpg"]},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplænɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large round object in space that moves around a star (such as the sun) and receives light from it","cn":"行星","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"the planets of our solar system","cn":"太阳系的行星"}},{"en":"used to mean ‘the world’, especially when talking about the environment","cn":"地球（尤指环境）","g":"[singular]","lab":"informal, humorous，，","ex":{"en":"the battle to save the planet","cn":"拯救地球的战斗"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"行星","en":"A planet is a large, round object in space that moves around a star. The Earth is a planet.","ex":{"en":"The picture shows six of the eight planets in the solar system.","cn":"这幅图标示了太阳系八大行星中的6颗。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He thinks being a father is easy. What planet is he on?","cn":"他认为做父亲很容易，他真是在做白日梦！"},{"en":"the battle to save the planet","cn":"拯救地球的战斗"}]},"plant":{"media":{"img":["media/ldoce/img/plant.jpg","media/pic/plantlabels_plants_comp.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/plant__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plant__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"plɑːnt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a living thing that grows in the earth and usually has a stem, leaves and roots, especially one that is smaller than a tree or bush","cn":"植物；花草","g":"[countable]","sc":"living thing","ex":{"en":"All plants need light and water.","cn":"一切植物都需要阳光和水。"}},{"en":"a factory or place where power is produced or an industrial process takes place","cn":"发电厂；工厂","g":"[countable]","sc":"factory","ex":{"en":"a nuclear power plant","cn":"核电站"}},{"en":"the large machines that are used in industrial processes","cn":"（工业用的）大型机器，设备","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"machines","ex":{"en":"The company has been investing in new plant and equipment.","cn":"这家公司一直在投资购置新机器和设备。"}},{"en":"something that somebody has deliberately placed among another person’s clothes or possessions in order to make them appear guilty of a crime","cn":"栽赃物品","g":"[countable, usually singular]","lab":"informal","sc":"something illegal","ex":{"en":"He claimed that the drugs found in his house were a plant.","cn":"他声称在他家中发现的毒品是一种植物。"}},{"en":"a person who joins a group of criminals or enemies in order to get and secretly report information about their activities","cn":"坐探；内线；卧底","g":"[countable]","sc":"person"},{"en":"to put plants, seeds, etc. in the ground to grow","cn":"栽种；种植；播种","sc":"seeds/plants","ex":{"en":"to plant a tree/seed/crop","cn":"种树；播种；种庄稼"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to cover or supply a garden, area of land, etc. with plants","cn":"在（某处）栽种","g":"[often passive]","sc":"seeds/plants","ex":{"en":"The children are planting a garden next to the school.","cn":"孩子们正在学校旁边的花园里栽种。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to place something or yourself in a particular place or position","cn":"放置；安放；站立","sc":"put in position","ex":{"en":"They planted a flag on the summit.","cn":"他们在山顶上插了一面旗子。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to hide something such as a bomb in a place where it will not be found","cn":"（秘密）放置，安置","sc":"bomb","pos":"verb"},{"en":"to hide something, especially something illegal, in somebody’s clothing, possessions, etc. so that when it is found it will look as though they committed a crime","cn":"（给某人）栽（赃）","sc":"something illegal","ex":{"en":"He claims that the drugs were planted on him.","cn":"他声称这些毒品是别人给他栽的赃。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to send somebody to join a group, etc., especially in order to make secret reports on its members","cn":"使卧底；安插（密探）","sc":"person","ex":{"en":"The police had planted an informer in the gang.","cn":"警方在该团伙中安插了一名线人。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make somebody think or believe something, especially without them realizing that you gave them the idea","cn":"（尤指潜移默化地）使（思想、信念等）植根于","sc":"thought/idea","ex":{"en":"He planted the first seeds of doubt in my mind.","cn":"是他最初启发我起疑心的。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"植物","en":"A plant is a living thing that grows in the earth and has a stem, leaves, and roots.","ex":{"en":"Water each plant as often as required.","cn":"按要求经常给每一株植物浇水。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"播（种）；种植；栽种","en":"When you plant a seed, plant, or young tree, you put it into the ground so that it will grow there.","ex":{"en":"He says he plans to plant fruit trees and vegetables.","cn":"他说他打算种植果树和蔬菜。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"在…种上植物（或农作物）","en":"When someone plants land with a particular type of plant or crop, they put plants, seeds, or young trees into the land to grow them there.","ex":{"en":"They plan to plant the area with grass and trees","cn":"他们计划在这一地区种草植树。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"工厂；发电厂","en":"A plant is a factory or a place where power is produced.","ex":{"en":"...Ford's British car assembly plants","cn":"福特公司在英国的汽车装配厂"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"成套机械；成套设备；成套装置","en":"Plant is large machinery that is used in industrial processes.","ex":{"en":"...investment in plant and equipment.","cn":"对机械设备的投资"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"安放；放置；使固定","en":"If you plant something somewhere, you put it there firmly.","ex":{"en":"She planted her feet wide and bent her knees slightly.","cn":"她双脚宽分站稳，膝盖微屈。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"藏放；埋设","en":"To plant something such as a bomb means to hide it somewhere so that it explodes or works there.","ex":{"en":"So far no one has admitted planting the bomb.","cn":"到目前为止，还没有人承认是自己放了炸弹。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"把（武器、毒品等）栽赃（于某人）","en":"If something such as a weapon or drugs is planted on someone, it is put among their possessions or in their house so that they will be wrongly accused of a crime.","ex":{"en":"He claimed that the drugs had been planted to incriminate him.","cn":"他声称毒品是有人栽赃陷害他。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"派遣；安插","en":"If an organization plants someone somewhere, they send that person there so that they can get information or watch someone secretly.","ex":{"en":"Journalists informed police who planted an undercover detective to trap Smith.","cn":"记者通知了警方，后者于是为诱捕史密斯而安插了一名卧底侦探。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"给，对着（某人一吻）","en":"If you plant a kiss on someone, you give them a kiss.","ex":{"en":"She planted a kiss on each of his leathery cheeks.","cn":"她在他粗糙的面颊上左右各吻了一下。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"灌输（思想）","en":"If you plant an idea in someone's mind, they begin to accept the idea without realizing that it has originally come from you and not from them.","ex":{"en":"He hoped that he could plant the idea in such a way that Abramov would believe it was his own.","cn":"他希望能把这个想法注入阿布拉莫夫的头脑，但要让他相信这是他自己的念头。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：plant out"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The company has been investing in new plant and equipment.","cn":"这家公司一直在投资购置新机器和设备。"},{"en":"He claims that the drugs were planted on him.","cn":"他声称这些毒品是别人给他栽的赃。"}]},"placing":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/placing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/placing__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪsɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the position of somebody/something in a race or a competition or in a list arranged in order of success","cn":"名次；排名","ex":{"en":"He needs a high placing in today's qualifier to reach the final.","cn":"在今天的资格赛中，他必须排名靠前才能进入决赛。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He needs a high placing in today's qualifier to reach the final.","cn":"在今天的资格赛中，他必须排名靠前才能进入决赛。"},{"en":"Hancock and Smith took the top two placings.","cn":"汉考克和史密斯排名前两位。"}],"base":"place"},"plow":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"→see: ;"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plow__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plow__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"plaʊ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large piece of farming equipment with one or several curved blades, (= metal cutting parts) pulled by a tractor or by animals. It is used for digging and turning over soil, especially before seeds are planted.","cn":"犁"},{"en":"to dig and turn over a field or other area of land with a plow","cn":"犁：用犁挖和翻开一块田地或其他土地","ex":{"en":"plowed fields","cn":"犁过的田地"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"platforms":{"lemma":"platform","media":{"img":["media/pic/shoes_comp.jpg","media/thumb/platform.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/platform__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/platform__us_1.mp3"}},"plastic":{"media":{"img":["media/pic/cupsandglasses_diningroom_comp.jpg","media/thumb/plastic.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/plastic__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plastic__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplæstɪk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a light strong material that is produced by chemical processes and can be formed into shapes when heated. There are many different types of plastic, used to make different objects and fabrics.","cn":"塑料","g":"[uncountable, countable, usually plural]","ex":{"en":"The pipes should be made of plastic.","cn":"这些管子应该是用塑料制作的。"}},{"en":"the science of making plastics","cn":"塑料学","g":"[uncountable]"},{"en":"a way of talking about credit cards","cn":"信用卡","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"Do they take plastic?","cn":"他们收信用卡吗？"}},{"en":"made of plastic","cn":"塑料制的；塑料的","ex":{"en":"a plastic bag/bottle/cup","cn":"塑料袋／瓶／杯"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"easily formed into different shapes","cn":"可塑的；有塑性的","ex":{"en":"Clay is a plastic substance.","cn":"黏土是可塑物质。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"that seems artificial; false; not real or sincere","cn":"做作的；虚伪的；矫饰的","lab":"disapproving","ex":{"en":"TV game show hosts with their banal remarks and plastic smiles","cn":"语言陈腐、笑容刻板的电视竞赛节目主持人"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-MASS 物质名词","cn":"塑料","en":"Plastic is a material which is produced from oil by a chemical process and which is used to make many objects. It is light in weight and does not break easily.","ex":{"en":"...a wooden crate, sheltered from wetness by sheets of plastic","cn":"用塑料薄膜防潮的木板箱"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"不自然的；不真实的","en":"If you describe something as plastic, you mean that you think it looks or tastes unnatural or not real.","ex":{"en":"...plastic airline food","cn":"航班上味同嚼蜡的食品"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（塑料制）信用卡","en":"If you use plastic or plastic money to pay for something, you pay for it with a credit card instead of using cash.","ex":{"en":"Using plastic to pay for an order is simplicity itself.","cn":"用信用卡支付订单是很简单的事。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"可塑的；塑性的","en":"Something that is plastic is soft and can easily be made into different shapes.","ex":{"en":"The mud is smooth, gray, soft, and plastic as butter.","cn":"这种泥浆呈灰色，它光滑、柔软，像黄油一样易塑。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"TV game show hosts with their banal remarks and plastic smiles","cn":"语言陈腐、笑容刻板的电视竞赛节目主持人"},{"en":"The pipes should be made of plastic.","cn":"这些管子应该是用塑料制作的。"}]},"pleasurable":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleʒərəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"giving pleasure","cn":"愉快的；快活的；适意的","ex":{"en":"a pleasurable experience","cn":"愉快的经历"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"令人愉快的；使人高兴的","en":"Pleasurable experiences or sensations are pleasant and enjoyable.","ex":{"en":"The most pleasurable experience of the evening was the wonderful fireworks display","cn":"这个晚上最让人高兴的就是精彩的焰火表演。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/pleasurable__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/pleasurable__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"We do everything we can to make your trip pleasurable.","cn":"我们会尽力使你的旅途愉快。"},{"en":"a pleasurable experience","cn":"愉快的经历"}]},"plunge":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plunge__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plunge__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"plʌndʒ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to move or make somebody/something move suddenly forwards and/or downwards","cn":"（使）突然前冲（或下落）","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"She lost her balance and plunged 100 feet to her death.","cn":"她没有站稳，从 100 英尺的高处跌下摔死了。"}},{"en":"to decrease suddenly and quickly","cn":"暴跌；骤降；突降","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Stock markets plunged at the news of the coup.","cn":"政变的消息一传来，股票市场便暴跌。"}},{"en":"to slope down steeply","cn":"陡峭地向下倾斜","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The track plunged down into the valley.","cn":"小路陡然而下，直插山谷。"}},{"en":"to move up and down suddenly and violently","cn":"（剧烈）颠簸，震荡","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"The horse plunged and reared.","cn":"马猛然跃起，用后腿直立。"}},{"en":"a sudden movement downwards or away from something","cn":"突然跌落；突然分离","ex":{"en":"The calm water ends there and the river begins a headlong plunge.","cn":"平静的河水突然中断，开始奔腾直泻而下。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a sudden decrease in an amount or the value of something","cn":"（数量、价格的）暴跌，猛降，骤减","pos":"noun"},{"en":"the act of becoming involved in a situation or activity","cn":"卷入；参与","ex":{"en":"The company is planning a deeper plunge into the commercial market.","cn":"这家公司正计划进一步投入商业市场。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"an act of jumping or diving into water; a quick swim","cn":"跳水；快速游泳","ex":{"en":"She went for a plunge.","cn":"她去游泳了。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（尤指向水中）纵身投入，一头进入","en":"If something or someone plunges in a particular direction, especially into water, they fall, rush, or throw themselves in that direction.","ex":{"en":"At least 50 people died when a bus plunged into a river","cn":"一辆公共汽车栽进河里，造成至少50人丧生。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"将…投入；将…插入；将…刺进","en":"If you plunge an object into something, you push it quickly or violently into it.","ex":{"en":"A soldier plunged a bayonet into his body","cn":"一名士兵将刺刀插进了他的身体。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"（使）突然陷入；（使）突然遭受","en":"If a person or thing is plunged into a particular state or situation, or if they plunge into it, they are suddenly in that state or situation.","ex":{"en":"The government's political and economic reforms threaten to plunge the country into chaos","cn":"政府的政治和经济改革可能会使国家陷入混乱局面。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"（使）投身；（使）突然开始从事","en":"If you plunge into an activity or are plunged into it, you suddenly get very involved in it.","ex":{"en":"The two men plunged into discussion","cn":"两位男士立即投入到讨论中。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"骤降；猛跌","en":"If an amount or rate plunges, it decreases quickly and suddenly.","ex":{"en":"His weight began to plunge","cn":"他的体重开始锐减。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"决定冒险尝试；采取断然行动","en":"If you take the plunge, you decide to do something that you consider difficult or risky.","ex":{"en":"If you have been thinking about buying shares, now could be the time to take the plunge.","cn":"如果你一直在考虑购买股票，现在或许是采取行动的最好时机。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She lost her balance and plunged 100 feet to her death.","cn":"她没有站稳，从 100 英尺的高处跌下摔死了。"},{"en":"The pool was declared open and eager swimmers plunged in.","cn":"游泳池刚刚宣布开门，游泳的人就急切地跳入池中。"}]},"plausible":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plausible__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plausible__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplɔːzəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"reasonable and likely to be true","cn":"有道理的；可信的","ex":{"en":"Her story sounded perfectly plausible.","cn":"她的说辞听起来言之有理。"}},{"en":"good at sounding honest and sincere, especially when trying to trick people","cn":"巧言令色的；花言巧语的","lab":"disapproving","ex":{"en":"She was a plausible liar.","cn":"她是个巧言令色的说谎高手。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（解释或说法）似乎真实的，貌似合理的","en":"An explanation or statement that is plausible seems likely to be true or valid.","ex":{"en":"A more plausible explanation would seem to be that people are fed up with the Conservative government","cn":"貌似更加合理的解释似乎是，人们已经厌倦了保守党政府。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（人）貌似可信的，花言巧语的","en":"If you say that someone is plausible, you mean that they seem to be telling the truth and to be sincere and honest.","ex":{"en":"He was so plausible that he conned everybody.","cn":"他那么会花言巧语，以至于骗过了所有的人。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He argued very plausibly that the claims were true.","cn":"他花言巧语地辩解说那些说法属实。"},{"en":"The only plausible explanation is that he forgot.","cn":"唯一合理的解释就是他忘掉了。"}]},"plays":{"lemma":"play","media":{"uk":"media/uk/play__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/play__us_1.mp3"}},"platoon":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/platoon__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/platoon__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pləˈtuːn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a small group of soldiers that is part of a company and commanded by a lieutenant","cn":"（军队的）排"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（通常由中尉指挥的）排","en":"A platoon is a small group of soldiers, usually one which is commanded by a lieutenant."}]}},"plum":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plum__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plum__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/plum.jpg"]},"oxford":{"phon":"plʌm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a soft round fruit with smooth red or purple skin, that is sweet inside with a large flat seed","cn":"李子；梅子","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a plum tree","cn":"李树"}},{"en":"a dark colour between red and purple","cn":"紫红色","g":"[uncountable, countable]"},{"en":"considered very good and worth having","cn":"称心的；值得拥有的","ex":{"en":"She's landed a plum job at the BBC.","cn":"她在英国广播公司谋得一份称心如意的工作。"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"李子；梅子","en":"A plum is a small, sweet fruit with a smooth red or yellow skin and a stone in the middle."},{"pos":"COLOUR 颜色词","cn":"紫红色；青紫色","en":"Something that is plum or plum-coloured is a dark reddish-purple colour.","ex":{"en":"...plum-coloured silk.","cn":"紫红色的丝绸"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（工作、合同、角色等）令人垂涎的，吸引人的","en":"A plum job, contract, or role is a very good one that a lot of people would like.","ex":{"en":"Laura landed a plum job with a smart art gallery.","cn":"劳拉在一家时尚画廊找到了份美差。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She's landed a plum job at the BBC.","cn":"她在英国广播公司谋得称心如意的工作。"},{"en":"a plum tree","cn":"李树"}]},"pleasing":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/pleasing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/pleasing__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpliːzɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that gives you pleasure or makes you feel satisfied","cn":"令人高兴的；令人满意的","ex":{"en":"a pleasing design","cn":"令人满意的设计"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"令人愉快的；使人满意的","en":"Something that is pleasing gives you pleasure and satisfaction.","ex":{"en":"This area of France has a pleasing climate in August","cn":"法国的这一地区在8月份气候宜人。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She had a pleasingly direct manner.","cn":"她为人直爽，令人愉快。"},{"en":"The new building was pleasing to the eye.","cn":"这座新楼真漂亮。"}],"base":"please"},"plaster":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplɑːstə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a substance made of lime, water and sand, that is put on walls and ceilings to give them a smooth hard surface","cn":"灰泥","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"an old house with crumbling plaster and a leaking roof","cn":"一所灰泥剥落、屋顶漏水的老房子"}},{"en":"a white powder that is mixed with water and becomes very hard when it dries, used especially for making copies of statues or holding broken bones in place","cn":"建筑石膏；熟石膏","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"less frequent","ex":{"en":"a plaster bust of Julius Caesar","cn":"一尊尤利乌斯·凯撒的半身石膏塑像"}},{"en":"a piece of material that can be stuck to the skin to protect a small wound or cut; this material","cn":"膏药；创可贴；护创胶布","g":"[countable, uncountable]","lab":"both British English","ex":{"en":"Have you got any plasters? I've cut my finger.","cn":"你有创可贴吗？我割破了手指。"}},{"en":"to cover a wall, etc. with plaster","cn":"抹灰于，用灰泥抹（墙等）","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"The walls need plastering before we can start decorating.","cn":"在我们开始装饰之前，墙壁需要抹灰。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to cover somebody/something with a wet or sticky substance","cn":"往…上涂抹","ex":{"en":"She plastered herself in suntan lotion.","cn":"她往身上抹防晒液。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make your hair flat and stick to your head","cn":"把（头发）梳平；使（头发）粘在（头上）","g":"[usually passive]","ex":{"en":"His wet hair was plastered to his head.","cn":"他那湿透的头发紧贴在头皮上。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to completely cover a surface with pictures or posters","cn":"贴满，遍贴（画片或招贴画）","g":"[often passive]","ex":{"en":"Her bedroom wall was plastered with photos of him.","cn":"她卧室的墙上贴满了他的照片。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"灰泥；灰浆；熟石膏","en":"Plaster is a smooth paste made of sand, lime, and water which goes hard when it dries. Plaster is used to cover walls and ceilings and is also used to make sculptures.","ex":{"en":"There were huge cracks in the plaster, and the green shutters were faded","cn":"灰泥上出现多条大裂缝，绿色百叶窗也褪色了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"涂灰泥于；在…上抹灰浆","en":"If you plaster a wall or ceiling, you cover it with a layer of plaster.","ex":{"en":"The ceiling he had just plastered fell in and knocked him off his ladder.","cn":"他刚抹上灰泥的天花板塌了，把他从梯子上砸了下来。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"在…上大量粘贴；贴满","en":"If you plaster a surface or a place with posters or pictures, you stick a lot of them all over it.","ex":{"en":"They plastered the city with posters condemning her election","cn":"他们在城里到处张贴谴责她当选的海报。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（给自己）涂上，抹上","en":"If you plaster yourself in some kind of sticky substance, you cover yourself in it.","ex":{"en":"She plastered herself from head to toe in high factor sun lotion.","cn":"她给自己从头到脚都抹上了强效防晒露。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"膏药；橡皮膏；创可贴","en":"A plaster is a strip of sticky material used for covering small cuts or sores on your body."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"打着石膏；上着筒形石膏夹","en":"If you have a leg or arm in plaster, you have a cover made of plaster of Paris around your leg or arm, in order to protect a broken bone and allow it to mend."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/plaster__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/plaster__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/first_aid_kit.jpg"]},"examples":[{"en":"The next day their picture was plastered all over the newspapers.","cn":"第二天，他们的照片被刊登在各家报纸上。"},{"en":"a plaster bust of Julius Caesar","cn":"一尊尤利乌斯 · 凯撒的半身石膏塑像"}]},"plains":{"lemma":"plain"},"pleasures":{"lemma":"pleasure"},"planned":{"lemma":"plan"},"placed":{"oxford":{"phon":"pleɪst","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"finishing among the winners (usually second or third)","cn":"名列前茅（通常指第二名或第三名）","ex":{"en":"The horse not only failed to win, it wasn't even placed.","cn":"这匹马不仅没有获胜，甚至没有获得名次。"}}]},"base":"place"},"plaques":{"lemma":"plaque"},"places":{"lemma":"place"},"plantings":{"lemma":"plant"},"plagues":{"lemma":"plague"},"planners":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplænə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person whose job is to plan the growth and development of a town","cn":"城市规划者"},{"en":"a person who makes plans for a particular area of activity","cn":"设计者；规划者"}]}},"plunged":{"lemma":"plunge"},"plans":{"lemma":"plan"},"plants":{"lemma":"plant"},"planted":{"lemma":"plant"},"played":{"lemma":"play"},"plasterers":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplɑːstərə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person whose job is to put plaster on walls and ceilings","cn":"抹灰工；泥水匠；粉刷工"}]}},"plumbers":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplʌmə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person whose job is to fit and repair things such as water pipes, toilets, etc.","cn":"水暖工；管子工；铅管工"}]}},"platefuls":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪtfʊl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the amount that a plate holds","cn":"一盘之量；盘"}]}},"plates":{"lemma":"plate"},"players":{"lemma":"player"},"plea":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"恳求；请求","en":"A plea is an appeal or request for something, made in an intense or emotional way.","ex":{"en":"Mr Nicholas made his emotional plea for help in solving the killing.","cn":"尼古拉斯先生恳请帮助以解决这起凶杀案。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（法庭上表明对于被指控的罪名服或不服的）申诉，答辩，抗辩","en":"In a court of law, a person's plea is the answer that they give when they have been charged with a crime, saying whether or not they are guilty of that crime.","ex":{"en":"The judge questioned him about his guilty plea","cn":"法官就他的认罪答辩进行审问。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"辩由；借口；托词","en":"A plea is a reason which is given, to a court of law or to other people, as an excuse for doing something or for not doing something.","ex":{"en":"Phillips murdered his wife, but got off on a plea of insanity","cn":"菲利普斯谋杀了他的妻子，但以精神错乱为由逃脱了惩罚。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a statement, letter etc in which you ask for something politely or formally","cn":""},{"en":"a strong request saying very clearly what you want, especially when you are asking for something that someone does not want to give you","cn":""},{"en":"a request for something, especially money, that someone thinks they have a legal right to have","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A plea is what you make when you're begging for something with a sense of urgency and emotion. While you wouldn't call asking for a hall pass a plea , you could make a plea for justice or world peace."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. desperate, dramatic, strong, urgent | heartfelt, impassioned, passionate | repeated | personal","VERB + PLEA make | ignore","PREP. despite a/the ~, in spite of a/the ~ Despite pleas from his mother, the gunman refused to give himself up. | ~ by/from Hospital visiti","ADJ. guilty | not guilty","VERB + PLEA enter | hear | change | accept, sustain The prosecution accepted a plea of manslaughter. | support | reject","PLEA + NOUN bargain, bargaining","PREP. ~ for A senior judge heard a plea for damages on behalf of the accident victims. | ~ of Her solicitor entered a plea of guilty on her "]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/7/plea0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/plea.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He was charged with murder, but got off on a plea of insanity.","cn":"他被指控犯了谋杀罪，但以精神错乱为由逃过惩罚。"},{"en":"He refused to listen to her tearful pleas.","cn":"他对她声泪俱下的恳求置之不理。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"pliː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a serious emotional request, especially for something needing action now","cn":"请求；恳求","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"She made an impassioned plea for help.","cn":"她恳切地求助。"}},{"en":"a statement made by somebody or for somebody who is accused of a crime","cn":"（被告或被告律师的）诉讼抗辩，答辩","lab":"law","ex":{"en":"a plea of guilty/not guilty","cn":"承认／不承认有罪"}},{"en":"a reason given to a court for doing or not doing something","cn":"（向法庭提供的）理由，借口，辩解","lab":"law","ex":{"en":"He was charged with murder, but got off on a plea of insanity.","cn":"他被指控犯了谋杀罪，但以精神错乱为由逃过惩罚。"}}]}},"plumbing":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（建筑物的）水管装置，水暖设备","en":"The plumbing in a building consists of the water and drainage pipes, baths, and toilets in it.","ex":{"en":"The electrics and the plumbing were sound.","cn":"电路和水暖设备都完好无损。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"水管工程；管道工程","en":"Plumbing is the work of connecting and repairing things such as water and drainage pipes, baths, and toilets.","ex":{"en":"She learned the rudiments of brick-laying, wiring and plumbing.","cn":"她学习了砌砖、布线和管道工程的基本知识。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the pipes that water flows through in a building 〔","cn":"建筑物内的〕管道系统"},{"en":"the work of fitting and repairing water pipes, baths, toilets etc","cn":"管道安装与维修工作"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. cold water, hot water | domestic, household","VERB + PLUMBING put in They're going to have to put in new plumbing.","PLUMBING + NOUN arrangements, system | fittings | tools | job, work | leak"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/plumbing0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/plumbing.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"We keep having problems with the plumbing.","cn":"我们的管道老是出问题。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplʌmɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the system of pipes, etc. that supply water to a building","cn":"（建筑物的）管路系统，自来水管道","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"The builders are putting in the plumbing and electrics.","cn":"建筑商正在安装管道和电力。"}},{"en":"the work of a plumber","cn":"水暖工的工作","ex":{"en":"the tools used in plumbing","cn":"管道工程中使用的工具"}}]}},"plaintiff":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"原告；起诉人","en":"A plaintiff is a person who brings a legal case against someone in a court of law."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who brings a legal action against another person in a court of law","cn":"起诉人﹐原告"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"In a courtroom, the plaintiff is the person or group who is accusing another person or group of some wrongdoing. If you’re the plaintiff , you are claiming that a law was broken, and you’re in court to present your case."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERB + PLAINTIFF compensate","PLAINTIFF + VERB bring an action (against sb), sue sb | allege sth, argue sth, claim sth, contend sth, seek sth, submit sth The plaintiff cl","PREP. against the ~ Costs were awarded against the plaintiff. | on behalf of the ~ the lawyer appearing on behalf of the plaintiff"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/plaintiff0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/plaintiff.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈpleɪntɪf","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who makes a formal complaint against somebody in court","cn":"原告；起诉人","ex":{"en":"The court upheld the plaintiff’s claim for damages.","cn":"法院支持了原告的损害赔偿请求。"}}]}},"pledge":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"保证；诺言；誓言","en":"When someone makes a pledge, they make a serious promise that they will do something.","ex":{"en":"The meeting ended with a pledge to step up cooperation between the six states of the region.","cn":"会议以承诺加快这一地区六国间的合作而结束。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"保证，许诺，发誓（做）；保证给予","en":"When someone pledges to do something, they promise in a serious way to do it. When they pledge something, they promise to give it.","ex":{"en":"Mr Dudley has pledged to give any award to charity","cn":"达德利先生已承诺将任何所获的损害赔偿额都捐给慈善机构。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"许诺拨（款）；许诺给予","en":"If you pledge a sum of money to an organization or activity, you promise to pay that amount of money to it at a particular time or over a particular period.","ex":{"en":"The French President is pledging $150 million in French aid next year","cn":"法国总统许诺为法国明年的援助经费拨款1.5亿美元。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使保证，使许诺，使发誓（遵循或支持）","en":"If you pledge yourself to something, you commit yourself to following a particular course of action or to supporting a particular person, group, or idea.","ex":{"en":"The President pledged himself to increase taxes for the rich but not the middle classes","cn":"总统保证增加对富人而非中产阶级的税收。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"用…抵押；以…典押","en":"If you pledge something such as a valuable possession or a sum of money, you leave it with someone as a guarantee that you will repay money that you have borrowed.","ex":{"en":"He asked her to pledge the house as security for a loan.","cn":"他要她拿房子来抵押贷款。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a statement that you will definitely do or provide something, which may not be reliable","cn":""},{"en":"a public or official promise to do a particular thing in the future","cn":""},{"en":"a very serious promise to do something or not to do something that you choose to make","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n v 2 n v 3 n v 4 ","senses":[{"en":"A pledge is basically very serious formal promise. You can pledge allegiance to your country, you can pledge to keep a secret, and you can pledge a sum of money to a cause."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. campaign, election, manifesto | spending spending pledges given by the government","VERB + PLEDGE give (sb), make, sign | fulfil, honour | betray, go back on, renege on","PREP. ~ on manifesto pledges on greater public spending","PHRASES a pledge of support"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/e/pledge_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/0/pledge1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Will the government honour its election pledge not to raise taxes?","cn":"政府会履行其竞选诺言，不增加税收吗？"},{"en":"Japan has pledged $100 million in humanitarian aid.","cn":"日本已承诺提供一亿元人道主义援助。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"pledʒ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to formally promise to give or do something","cn":"保证给予（或做）；正式承诺","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Japan has pledged $100 million in humanitarian aid.","cn":"日本已承诺提供一亿美元人道主义援助。"}},{"en":"to make somebody or yourself formally promise to do something","cn":"使保证；使发誓","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"They were all pledged to secrecy.","cn":"他们都宣誓保密。"}},{"en":"to leave something with somebody as a pledge","cn":"抵押；典当","g":"[transitive]"},{"en":"to promise to become a junior member of a fraternity or sorority","cn":"宣誓参加美国大学生联谊会","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"Do you think you'll pledge this semester?","cn":"这学期你会加入大学生联谊会吗？"}},{"en":"a serious promise","cn":"保证；诺言；誓约","ex":{"en":"a pledge of support","cn":"支援的许诺"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a sum of money or something valuable that you leave with somebody to prove that you will do something or pay back money that you owe","cn":"质钱；抵押品","pos":"noun"}]}},"plateau":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"高原","en":"A plateau is a large area of high and fairly flat land.","ex":{"en":"A broad valley opened up leading to a high, flat plateau of cultivated land.","cn":"一条宽阔的山谷展现在眼前，通往一处平整的开垦地高原。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（活动或进程中的）稳定阶段，停滞时期","en":"If you say that an activity or process has reached a plateau, you mean that it has reached a stage where there is no further change or development.","ex":{"en":"The US heroin market now appears to have reached a plateau","cn":"美国的海洛因市场现在似乎已到了停滞期。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（活动、进程、成本等）达到稳定阶段，进入停滞时期","en":"If something such as an activity, process, or cost plateaus or plateaus out, it reaches a stage where there is no further change or development.","ex":{"en":"Evelyn's career is accelerating, and mine is plateauing out a bit","cn":"伊夫琳的职业生涯蒸蒸日上，而我的则停滞不前。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large area of flat land that is higher than the land around it","cn":"高原"},{"en":"a period during which the level of something does not change, especially after a period when it was increasing","cn":"平稳时期﹐〔尤指某物增长后的〕稳定期"},{"en":"if something plateaus, it reaches and then stays at a particular level","cn":"达到稳定水平[阶段]"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A plateau is a high, flat area of land. The word has also been stretched to include a leveling off of progress––for a while the eighth graders having a sleepover were crazy, then their energy level reached a plateau ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. high | broad, rolling, vast | central","VERB + PLATEAU reach (figurative) The children's standard of reading seems to have reached a plateau (= they are not making any more progres","PLATEAU + VERB overlook sth","PREP. across a/the ~ A terrible storm swept across the plateau."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/plateau_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/plateau.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Unemployment has at last plateaued out.","cn":"失业情况终于稳定了下来。"},{"en":"Inflation has reached a plateau.","cn":"通货膨胀停了下来。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈplætəʊ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an area of flat land that is higher than the land around it","cn":"高原","ex":{"en":"The summit is a windswept plateau of scattered rocks.","cn":"山顶暴风肆虐，碎石散布。"}},{"en":"a time of little or no change after a period of growth or progress","cn":"（发展、增长后的）稳定期，停滞期","ex":{"en":"Inflation has reached a plateau.","cn":"通货膨胀停了下来。"}},{"en":"to stay at a steady level after a period of growth or progress","cn":"（在一段时期的发展后）保持稳定水平，处于停滞状态","ex":{"en":"Unemployment has at last plateaued out.","cn":"失业情况终于稳定了下来。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"plight":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"困境；苦境","en":"If you refer to someone's plight, you mean that they are in a difficult or distressing situation that is full of problems.","ex":{"en":"...the worsening plight of Third World countries plagued by debts.","cn":"受债务困扰的第三世界国家日益加深的苦境"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the situation you are in, for example how much money you earn, where you live, whether you are married or have children etc","cn":""},{"en":"your personal situation, for example how much money you earn, where you live, whether you are married or have children etc - used especially in official contexts","cn":""},{"en":"the situation that someone is in, especially a difficult or embarrassing situation that restricts what they can do","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 v n","senses":[{"en":"A plight is a situation that's hard to get out of. Learning about the plight of very poor people trying rebuild their homes after a devastating earthquake might inspire you to send money to a charity."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. desperate, sad, sorry, tragic the desperate plight of flood victims | economic, financial","VERB + PLIGHT recognize, see | draw attention to, highlight, publicize He has been sleeping rough in the streets to highlight the plight of "]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/plight_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/plight1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The African elephant is in a desperate plight.","cn":"非洲象正面临绝境。"},{"en":"the plight of the homeless","cn":"无家可归者的艰难困苦"}],"oxford":{"phon":"plaɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a difficult and sad situation","cn":"苦难；困境；苦境","ex":{"en":"the plight of homeless people","cn":"无家可归者的困境"}}]}},"plutonium":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"钚（尤用于核武器及用作核电站燃料的一种放射性元素）","en":"Plutonium is a radioactive element used especially in nuclear weapons and as a fuel in nuclear power stations."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a radioactive metal that is used in the production of nuclear power, and in nuclear weapons. It is a chemical element : symbol Pu","cn":"钚〔一种化学元素﹐符号为Pu〕"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. radioactive | civil | military, weapons-grade","VERB + PLUTONIUM extract, produce, recover one tonne of plutonium extracted from spent nuclear fuel","PLUTONIUM + NOUN fuel"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/plutonium0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/plutonium.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"pluːˈtəʊniəm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a chemical element. Plutonium is radioactive and is used in nuclear weapons and in producing nuclear energy.","cn":"钚（放射性化学元素）","ex":{"en":"the capability to enrich uranium or reprocess plutonium","cn":"浓缩铀或再处理钚的能力"}}]}},"plead":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"恳求；请求","en":"If you plead with someone to do something, you ask them in an intense, emotional way to do it.","ex":{"en":"The lady pleaded with her daughter to come back home","cn":"这位女士恳求她的女儿回家。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"作（有罪或无罪的）答辩","en":"When someone charged with a crime pleads guilty or not guilty in a court of law, they officially state that they are guilty or not guilty of the crime.","ex":{"en":"Morris had pleaded guilty to robbery.","cn":"莫里斯已承认犯有抢劫罪。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"为…辩护；维护；声援","en":"If you plead the case or cause of someone or something, you speak out in their support or defence.","ex":{"en":"He appeared before the Committee to plead his case","cn":"他出现在委员会面前为自己辩护。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"提出…为理由；把…作为借口","en":"If you plead a particular thing as the reason for doing or not doing something, you give it as your excuse.","ex":{"en":"Mr Burke, pleading poverty, changed his mind","cn":"伯克先生以自己穷为由改变了主意。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to tell someone you want them to give you something","cn":""},{"en":"to ask for food or drink in a restaurant","cn":""},{"en":"to ask for something in a firm way, insisting that someone gives you what you ask for","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To plead with someone is to try to convince them to see it your way. Your kids may plead with you to let them go on the super-huge outrageous roller coaster built in 1968, but you know better."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. almost She was almost pleading with him. | silently | successfully She successfully pleaded their cause with the mayor.","PREP. for They pleaded for mercy. | with His eyes silently pleaded with her. 2 say that you are guilty/not guilty","PHRASES plead guilty/not guilty He pleaded not guilty to the murder."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/plead0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/plead.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He advised his client to plead insanity (= say that he/she was mentally ill and therefore not responsible for his/her actions).","cn":"他建议他的当事人以精神不正常作为辩护理由。"},{"en":"He pleaded family problems for his lack of concentration.","cn":"他解释说他不能集中精神是因为有家庭问题。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"pliːd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to ask somebody for something in a very strong and serious way","cn":"乞求；恳求","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"She pleaded with him not to go.","cn":"她恳求他不要离开。"}},{"en":"to state in court that you are guilty or not guilty of a crime","cn":"（向法庭）表明认罪（或不认罪）","g":"[intransitive, transitive, no passive]","ex":{"en":"to plead guilty/not guilty","cn":"认罪；不认罪"}},{"en":"to present a case to a court","cn":"（在法庭上）申辩，辩护","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"They hired a top lawyer to plead their case.","cn":"他们聘请了一位顶级律师帮他们辩护。"}},{"en":"to argue in support of somebody/something","cn":"为…辩护；声援；支持","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","ex":{"en":"She appeared on television to plead the cause of political prisoners everywhere.","cn":"她出现在电视上为所有政治犯声援请命。"}},{"en":"to give something as an explanation or excuse for something","cn":"解释；推说；找借口","g":"[transitive, no passive]","ex":{"en":"He pleaded family problems for his lack of concentration.","cn":"他解释说他不能集中精神是因为有家庭问题。"}}]}},"ploy":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"计策；计谋；手段","en":"A ploy is a way of behaving that someone plans carefully and secretly in order to gain an advantage for themselves.","ex":{"en":"Christmas should be a time of excitement and wonder, not a cynical marketing ploy.","cn":"圣诞节应该是兴奋和美妙的时刻，而不该是一种肆无忌惮的营销策略。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a clever way of gaining an advantage, for example by making people feel concerned about you or making them feel grateful towards you","cn":""},{"en":"something that is intended to achieve a particular aim, especially an aim that is slightly dishonest or unacceptable","cn":""},{"en":"clever ways of getting an advantage, especially by doing something that is unusual or secret","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A ploy is a clever plan that helps you get what you want. A manipulative little girl might shed tears simply as a ploy to get her mother to buy her ice cream."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. clever, effective, good, useful | deliberate, tactical | favourite, old, usual | marketing, sales","VERB + PLOY resort to, try","PLOY + VERB work","PREP. ~ for a ploy for deflecting criticism"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/ploy0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/ploy.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It was all a ploy to distract attention from his real aims.","cn":"那全是障眼法，借以转移对他真实目的的注意。"},{"en":"a clever marketing ploy","cn":"巧妙的销售策略"}],"oxford":{"phon":"plɔɪ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"words or actions that are carefully planned to get an advantage over somebody else","cn":"计谋；策略；手法；花招","ex":{"en":"a clever marketing ploy","cn":"巧妙的销售策略"}}]}},"plaque":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"匾额；饰板","en":"A plaque is a flat piece of metal or stone with writing on it which is fixed to a wall or other structure to remind people of an important person or event.","ex":{"en":"After touring the hospital, Her Majesty unveiled a commemorative plaque.","cn":"女王陛下巡视完这家医院后，为纪念匾揭了幕。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"牙斑；齿菌斑","en":"Plaque is a substance containing bacteria that forms on the surface of your teeth.","ex":{"en":"Deposits of plaque build up between the tooth and the gum.","cn":"牙齿和牙龈之间会滋生牙斑。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a piece of flat metal, wood, or stone with writing on it, used as a prize in a competition or attached to a building to remind people of an event or person","cn":"匾牌﹐匾额〔用于奖励或纪念〕"},{"en":"a harmful substance which forms on your teeth, which bacteria can live and breed in","cn":"牙（菌）斑"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 n","senses":[{"en":"A plaque is a sign that memorializes a person or event, such as the plaque on a building noting the person it's named after or the year it was built."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. commemorative, memorial","VERB + PLAQUE put up The local historical society put up a plaque at the site of the battle. | unveil","PLAQUE + VERB be dedicated to sb, commemorate sb/sth, honour sb | mark sth, record sth A plaque marks the place where the first printing pre","PREP. on a/the ~ Some Latin words were engraved on the plaque. | ~ on a plaque on the wall | ~ to There is a commemorative plaque to the art","ADJ. dental","VERB + PLAQUE remove","PLAQUE + VERB accumulate, build up"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/7/plaque0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/plaque.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The team’s coach was given a plaque.","cn":"那个队的教练得到一块匾牌。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"plæk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a flat piece of stone, metal, etc., usually with a name and dates on, attached to a wall in memory of a person or an event","cn":"（纪念性的）牌匾，匾额；纪念匾","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"A bronze plaque marks the house where the poet was born.","cn":"一块纪念铜匾标示出诗人出生的那所房屋。"}},{"en":"a soft substance that forms on teeth and encourages the growth of harmful bacteria","cn":"牙菌斑","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Remove plaque by brushing your teeth regularly.","cn":"定期刷牙去除牙菌斑。"}}]}},"plantation":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（尤指在热带国家的）种植园，大农场","en":"A plantation is a large piece of land, especially in a tropical country, where crops such as rubber, coffee, tea, or sugar are grown.","ex":{"en":"...banana plantations in Costa Rica.","cn":"哥斯达黎加的香蕉种植园"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"人造林","en":"A plantation is a large number of trees that have been planted together.","ex":{"en":"...a plantation of almond trees.","cn":"人造扁桃树林"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an area of land, used for growing crops or keeping animals","cn":""},{"en":"a very large farm in the western US, Canada, or South America where sheep, cattle, or horses are bred","cn":""},{"en":"a piece of land used for farming, that is smaller than an ordinary farm","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A plantation is a large agricultural property dedicated to planting a few crops on a large scale. If you dream of having 3,000 acres to raise cucumbers on, then you have dreams of a cucumber plantation ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. coconut, coffee, cotton, rubber, sugar, tea, etc.","VERB + PLANTATION work (on) Hundreds of slaves worked on the plantations.","PLANTATION + NOUN owner, worker | economy | house 2 land planted with trees","ADJ. conifer, eucalyptus, etc. | forestry","PREP. ~ of a plantation of oaks"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/plantation0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/plantation.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"conifer/forestry plantations","cn":"针叶树林地；种植林"},{"en":"a banana plantation","cn":"香蕉种植园"}],"oxford":{"phon":"plɑːnˈteɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large area of land, especially in a hot country, where crops such as coffee, sugar, rubber, etc. are grown","cn":"种植园，种植场（尤指热带国家种植咖啡、甘蔗、橡胶等的大庄园）","ex":{"en":"a banana/coffee plantation","cn":"香蕉／咖啡种植园"}},{"en":"a large area of land that is planted with trees to produce wood","cn":"木材林地；人造林","ex":{"en":"conifer/forestry plantations","cn":"针叶树林地；种植林"}}]}},"plague":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"瘟疫；疫病","en":"A plague is a very infectious disease that spreads quickly and kills large numbers of people.","ex":{"en":"A cholera plague had been killing many prisoners of war at the time.","cn":"当时霍乱疫情已在夺去很多战俘的生命。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（腺）鼠疫；黑死病","en":"Plague or the plague is a very infectious disease which usually results in death. The patient has a severe fever and swellings on his or her body.","ex":{"en":"...a fresh outbreak of plague.","cn":"新一轮鼠疫的爆发"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（某一事物肆虐造成的）灾难，祸患","en":"A plague of unpleasant things is a large number of them that arrive or happen at the same time.","ex":{"en":"The city is under threat from a plague of rats","cn":"该市处于鼠患的威胁之下。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"烦扰；令人头痛的事物","en":"If you describe something as a plague, you mean that it causes a great deal of trouble or harm.","ex":{"en":"Inflation will remain a recurrent plague","cn":"通货膨胀将继续成为周期性的烦扰。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"困扰；使烦恼；折磨","en":"If you are plagued by unpleasant things, they continually cause you a lot of trouble or suffering.","ex":{"en":"She was plagued by weakness, fatigue, and dizziness","cn":"她感觉体虚、疲倦、头昏眼花。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"缠扰；纠缠","en":"If someone plagues you, they keep bothering you or asking you for something.","ex":{"en":"I'm not going to plague you with a lot more questions, Miss Culver","cn":"卡尔弗小姐，我不会再问更多的问题来烦你了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"极力回避","en":"If you say that you avoid someone or something like the plague, you are emphasizing that you deliberately avoid them completely.","ex":{"en":"I would avoid him like the plague when his wife and my parents were around","cn":"他的妻子和我的父母在旁边时，我会极力躲着他。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"…真该死；愿上天降祸于…","en":"You say a plague on a particular person or thing when you are very irritated by them and do not want to bother with them any more.","ex":{"en":"A plague on you and your damned percentages!","cn":"你和你该死的百分比都见鬼去吧！"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a disease that causes death and spreads quickly to a large number of people","cn":"瘟疫﹐疫病"},{"en":"a very infectious disease that produces high fever and swollen places on the body, and often leads to death, especially bubonic plague","cn":"鼠疫〔尤指腺鼠疫〕"},{"en":"an uncontrolled and harmful increase in the numbers of a particular animal or insect","cn":"鼠灾/蝗灾等"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 n v 3 n v","senses":[{"en":"When the homeowner described her ant problem as a plague , the exterminator thought she was being a bit melodramatic. After all, a few bugs aren't exactly a huge calamity."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. bubonic | great Nearly a third of the population died in the Great Plague.","QUANT. outbreak a decline in population following outbreaks of plague","VERB + PLAGUE suffer The region has just suffered a plague of locusts. | be decimated by, be destroyed by","PLAGUE + VERB break out, start, strike (sth) Bubonic plague struck London in 1665. | spread","PREP. ~ of The city is suffering a plague of rats. •"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/f/plague_v0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/plague1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Rock stars have to get used to being plagued by autograph hunters.","cn":"摇滚歌星必须习惯歌迷要求签名的纠缠。"},{"en":"The team has been plagued by injury this season.","cn":"本赛季这支队一直为队员受伤所困扰。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"pleɪɡ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a disease spread by rats that causes a high temperature, swellings (= areas that are larger and rounder than usual) on the body and usually death","cn":"腺鼠疫","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a decline in population following outbreaks of plague","cn":"瘟疫爆发后人口的下降"}},{"en":"any disease that spreads quickly and kills a lot of people","cn":"瘟疫；烈性传染病","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"the plague of AIDS","cn":"艾滋病这种严重的传染病"}},{"en":"large numbers of an animal or insect that come into an area and cause great damage","cn":"（大批动物或昆虫肆虐造成的）灾害，祸患","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a plague of locusts/rats, etc.","cn":"蝗灾、鼠害等"}},{"en":"to cause pain or trouble to somebody/something over a period of time","cn":"给…造成长时间的痛苦（或麻烦）；困扰；折磨；使受煎熬","ex":{"en":"to be plagued by doubt","cn":"为疑虑所困扰"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to annoy somebody or create problems, especially by asking for something, demanding attention, etc.","cn":"纠缠；缠磨；缠扰","ex":{"en":"Rock stars have to get used to being plagued by autograph hunters.","cn":"摇滚歌星必须习惯歌迷要求签名的纠缠。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"plough":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"犁","en":"A plough is a large farming tool with sharp blades which is pulled across the soil to turn it over, usually before seeds are planted."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"犁（地）；耕（地）","en":"When someone ploughs an area of land, they turn over the soil using a plough.","ex":{"en":"They ploughed nearly 100,000 acres of virgin moorland.","cn":"他们犁了将近10万英亩未开垦的高沼地。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（土地）被开垦成耕地","en":"If an area of land is under the plough, it is used for growing crops. If land is brought or put under the plough, it is ploughed for the first time and is then used for growing crops.","ex":{"en":"There was not one inch of soil that was not under the plough.","cn":"没有一寸土地未被开垦成耕地。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to plough a furrow→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：plough back plough into plough on plough through plough up"}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a piece of farm equipment used to turn over the earth so that seeds can be planted","cn":"犁"},{"en":"land that is under the plough is used for growing crops 〔","cn":"土地〕用于耕种的"},{"en":"to make a hole in the ground using your hands, a tool, or a machine","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. heavy","VERB + PLOUGH draw, pull They need two horses to pull these heavy ploughs. | guide","PLOUGH + NOUN boy, team | furrow"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/9/plough0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/plough.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"No one was listening to her, but she ploughed on regardless.","cn":"没有人在听她讲话，但她仍不加理会，喋喋不休。"},{"en":"The government has ploughed more than $20 billion into building new schools.","cn":"政府已投放 200 多亿元兴建新学校。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"plaʊ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large piece of farming equipment with one or several curved blades (= metal cutting parts), pulled by a tractor or by animals. It is used for digging and turning over soil, especially before seeds are planted.","cn":"犁","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Oxen were used to pull ploughs.","cn":"牛被用来拉犁。"}},{"en":"a group of seven bright stars that can only be seen from the northern half of the world","cn":"北斗星","g":"[singular]","lab":"British English"},{"en":"to dig and turn over a field or other area of land with a plough","cn":"犁（田）；耕（地）；翻（土）","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"ploughed fields","cn":"犁过的田地"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"plank":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"厚（木）板；板条","en":"A plank is a long, flat, rectangular piece of wood.","ex":{"en":"It was very strong, made of three solid planks of wood.","cn":"它由3块坚固的木板做成，很结实。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（团体或政党的）政纲条目；（政策或纲领的）要点","en":"The main plank of a particular group or political party is the main principle on which it bases its policy, or its main aim.","ex":{"en":"Encouraging people to shop locally is a central plank of his environment policy.","cn":"他的环境政策的核心是鼓励人们购买当地产品。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a long narrow piece of wooden board, used especially for making structures to walk on （","cn":"厚）木板﹐板条"},{"en":"one of the main features or principles of an argument etc 〔","cn":"论证等的〕要点﹐核心"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. timber, wooden | loose | rotten","PHRASES a plank of wood"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/plank0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/plank.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The central plank of the bill was rural development.","cn":"这一法案的核心是农村发展。"},{"en":"a plank of wood","cn":"一块木板条"}],"oxford":{"phon":"plæŋk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a long narrow flat piece of wood that is used for making floors, etc.","cn":"木板；板条","ex":{"en":"a plank of wood","cn":"一长条木板"}},{"en":"a main point in the policy of an organization, especially a political party","cn":"（政党等的）政策准则，政纲的核心","ex":{"en":"The central plank of the bill was rural development.","cn":"这一法案的核心是农村发展。"}},{"en":"an exercise in which you lie on your stomach and raise your body off the ground by pressing down on your hands until your arms are straight and then hold that position for a fixed period of time","cn":"平板支撑（俯卧，双手下压，手臂伸直，将身体撑起离开地面，保持此姿势一定时间）","ex":{"en":"I do exercises to strengthen my stomach muscles, like push-ups and planks.","cn":"我会做增强腹肌的练习动作，比如俯卧撑和平板支撑。"}}]}},"platonic":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（恋爱等）柏拉图式的，纯精神而无肉欲的","en":"Platonic relationships or feelings of affection do not involve sex.","ex":{"en":"She values the platonic friendship she has had with Chris for ten years.","cn":"她珍惜自己和克里斯之间长达10年的柏拉图式的友情。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（古希腊哲学家）柏拉图的；柏拉图哲学的","en":"Platonic means relating to the ideas of the Greek philosopher Plato.","ex":{"en":"...the Platonic tradition of Greek philosophy.","cn":"希腊哲学的柏拉图传统"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"someone who has never had sex","cn":""},{"en":"someone who is celibate has chosen not to have sex at all, especially for religious reasons","cn":""},{"en":"a platonic relationship is one between people who do not have sex with each other, but are just friends - use this especially when other people think they are having a sexual relationship","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Platonic describes a relationship that is purely spiritual and not physical. If a guy and a girl hang out all the time but aren't boyfriend and girlfriend, they'd describe their friendship as platonic ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be | become | remain","ADV. purely, strictly Their friendship remained purely platonic."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/platonic0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/a/platonic.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Their relationship is strictly platonic.","cn":"他们的关系完全是纯友谊。"},{"en":"platonic love","cn":"柏拉图式的爱"}],"oxford":{"phon":"pləˈtɒnɪk","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"friendly but not involving sex","cn":"柏拉图式的（指不含性爱）","ex":{"en":"platonic love","cn":"柏拉图式的爱"}}]}}});
